मण्डलम् मध्यरूप ॥ ॰ ir — the port of crates/sadhana/src/t1/ir.rs

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE INTERMEDIATE REPRESENTATION, task D-002d, doc 03 §8.
॰
॰ It takes what व्याकर parsed — घोषणाकोश, and वास्तु's अभिव्यञ्जककोश and
॰ वाक्यकोश behind it — and lays out functions, basic blocks and a linear
॰ instruction stream for उत्सर्जन (D-002e) to allocate registers over.
॰
॰ ── WHAT THIS FILE REPLACES ──
॰ Every line here is new. The file that stood here was tools/port_encode.py
॰ output: it matched `pub struct` and nothing else, so it carried eight
॰ structs, two गणना and ONE routine, and that routine was a stub. Its names
॰ were letter-by-letter transliterations (इनसतटरउकशअन for Instruction) and
॰ its CONTENT did not match ir.rs at all — it declared DeviceLoad, Alloca,
॰ Mul, Div, Icmp and a conditional branch, none of which exist in the Rust
॰ original, and it omitted the (ValueId, Instruction) pairing that does.
॰ The generator now refuses to run. This file is hand-written from ir.rs.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAMES ── attested words from spec/lexicon.src.tsv wherever the
॰ lexicon has one: आज्ञा instruction, मूल्य value, वृत्ति function,
॰ लक्ष्यम् target, लङ्घनम् jump, संख्यानम् count, आह्वानम् call,
॰ प्रत्यागमनम् return. पर्व — a joint, the unit a book divides into — is
॰ derived, for the basic block; खण्ड was not free, वास्तु already spends it
॰ on the slice type constructor.
॰
॰ ── ON GROUPING ── spec/grammar-t1.ebnf freezes आरभ्य ॱ समाप्तम्,
॰ आदि ॱ इति and अङ्कः ॱ अन्तः but says out loud that OPERATORS AND THEIR
॰ PRECEDENCE ARE NOT FROZEN, and both readings are present in this crate
॰ today. Every order-dependent expression below is bracketed, so the file
॰ means one thing under either eventual rule. संयोजन does the same.
॰
॰ ── ON THE ARENAS ── Rust holds Vec<Function>, Vec<(ValueId, Instruction)>
॰ and HashMap<BlockId, Block>. T1 has neither a growable collection nor a
॰ map. This file does NOT invent an answer: it adopts the one व्याकर
॰ already uses — a preallocated कोश plus a module-level सूचकाङ्क that the
॰ appending routine advances. The HashMap needs no substitute at all, since
॰ its key is a dense counter, so the map IS an array INDEXED BY BLOCK ID: a
॰ वृत्ति records the first id and the count, and उत्सर्जन walks that run as
॰ Rust walks the sorted keys. THIS USED TO SAY "appended in key order", and
॰ that stopped being true with `W-198`: blocks are CLOSED in an order that
॰ is not their creation order — a यदि numbers then, else and join before it
॰ builds the then-body, and a nested यदि inside that body closes ITS blocks
॰ before the outer else is reached — so पर्वयोजनम् is Rust's
॰ `blocks.insert(id, block)` literally, a KEYED write at अङ्कन ॱ क्रमाङ्क,
॰ and not an appender. The interpreter grows an arena to any index written
॰ (`nirvahana.rs:914`), which is what makes a keyed write possible at all.
॰ THE ALLOCATOR QUESTION IS STILL OPEN — व्याकर's कोश are declared भवति ०
॰ and grown by writing past the index, and this file inherits that and no
॰ more. संयोजन refused the same convention for its two loops and said so;
॰ the difference is that व्याकर, the module this one reads FROM, has
॰ already committed to it, and a second convention in the same pipeline
॰ would be worse than the one that is there.
॰
॰ ── ON INDEX ZERO ── व्याकर's arenas are 1-based: योजनम् advances the
॰ सूचकाङ्क before it writes, so ० is never a live entry and ० therefore
॰ means ABSENT. Rust's ValueId and BlockId count from 0 and use Option for
॰ absence. This port keeps व्याकर's convention rather than Rust's, so that
॰ Option<ValueId> is a मूल्याङ्क whose क्रमाङ्क is ० and Option<Terminator>
॰ is an अवसान whose भेद is ०. One mechanism, and it is the sibling's.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS NOT PORTED ── named at the foot of the file with the routine
॰ that waits on each. None is a stub returning अपूर्णम्: they are arms
॰ MISSING from routines that otherwise work, which is why they are
॰ described where they belong rather than counted as unimplemented
॰ functions. All four — (a) to (d) — are closed and kept; what the builder
॰ still stubs is COUNTED by cause in `अपूर्णगणनाकोश` (`W-245`), not listed.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

आयातः वास्तु ।
आयातः व्याकर ।
आयातः पदविभाग ।
आयातः अक्षरकोश ।
॰ `W-237`: the resolver's symbol-kind arena (`अर्थ ॱ संज्ञाभेदकोश`, `W-228`) is
॰ what tells a routine's bare name from a variable's — see the नाम arm of
॰ अभिव्यञ्जकरचना. Read, never written, and only at a node the resolver
॰ placed a symbol on; a program the resolver never ran on reaches no read.
आयातः अर्थ ।
॰ `W-279`: the shared declaration store, for the cross-module field ordinal.
आयातः घोषणासञ्चय ।


॰ ══════════════════ instruction kinds ══════════════════
॰ Rust writes Instruction as an enum whose variants carry payloads. T1 has
॰ no tagged union with fields — संघः is a reserved word the grammar does
॰ not define — so the tag is an integer and the payloads are fields of one
॰ flat struct, which is what वास्तु does for अभिव्यञ्जक and वाक्य and what
॰ सङ्केतन does for its slot kinds. ० is not a kind: it means ABSENT.

सार्वजनिक चरः ध्रुवाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।      ॰ Instruction::ConstInt(i64)
सार्वजनिक चरः आह्वानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।     ॰ Instruction::Call(SymbolId, Vec<ValueId>)
सार्वजनिक चरः योगाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।       ॰ Instruction::Add(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः वियोगाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।     ॰ Instruction::Sub(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः प्राचलाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।    ॰ Instruction::Param(usize)
॰ `W-245` — THE FORMS THAT MAKE A STATUS MORE THAN ZERO. Eleven kinds, added
॰ to `ir.rs` and here in the same commit. The eight operators are the ones
॰ ADR-0032 froze, one kind each AS THE ISA HAS THEM (गुणनम् भागः शेषः
॰ वामसरणम् दक्षिणसरणम् युक्तम् विकल्पः वैषम्यम्); the three that are the M
॰ extension assemble and `yantra` does not execute them — a program that
॰ reaches one halts naming the word, and the census counts it. तुलना is
॰ ADR-0008's six conditions with the sub-kind in `उपभेद`; आहार and निधान
॰ are a LOCAL's read and write — a routine's `चरः` and its parameters live in
॰ frame SLOTS (`स्थानक्रम`), because the corpus assigns them inside `यावत्`
॰ bodies and a value that changes on a back-edge needs a join this IR has
॰ not got, while a slot needs nothing the emitter does not already address.
सार्वजनिक चरः गुणनाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।      ॰ Instruction::Mul(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः भागाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ ।       ॰ Instruction::Div(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः शेषाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ८ ।       ॰ Instruction::Rem(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः वामसरणाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९ ।    ॰ Instruction::Shl(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः दक्षिणसरणाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १० । ॰ Instruction::Shr(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः युक्ताज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ११ ।     ॰ Instruction::And(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः विकल्पाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १२ ।    ॰ Instruction::Or(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः वैषम्याज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १३ ।    ॰ Instruction::Xor(ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः तुलनाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १४ ।      ॰ Instruction::Cmp(CmpOp, ValueId, ValueId)
सार्वजनिक चरः आहाराज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १५ ।      ॰ Instruction::Load(usize)
सार्वजनिक चरः निधानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १६ ।     ॰ Instruction::Store(usize, ValueId)
॰ `W-254` — Instruction::ConstStr(Vec<u8>). A string literal's octets, and the
॰ value is their ADDRESS: `artha.t1:679` types a literal as a slice of unsigned
॰ octets and ADR-0026 makes a slice ONE address-sized word, so this defines a
॰ single मूल्याङ्क like every other kind. The octets themselves are a run in
॰ पाठाक्षरकोश below, because they are not a contiguous span of the source
॰ whenever ADR-0011's doubling occurs — see पाठाज्ञायोजनम्.
सार्वजनिक चरः पाठाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १७ ।       ॰ Instruction::ConstStr(Vec<u8>)
॰ १८, AND NOT १९ AS FIRST WRITTEN. `ir.rs`'s `LoadField` margin reserved १८ for
॰ itself, which is not a thing this numbering supports: `the_kind_table_scan_is_not_vacuous`
॰ asserts the kinds are CONTIGUOUS १..=N, so a number reserved by prose and
॰ declared nowhere leaves a hole the guard refuses. A kind is claimed by being
॰ declared here, in the order things land — `LoadField` takes the next one when
॰ its own half arrives.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १८ ।    ॰ Instruction::LoadGlobal(SymbolId)
॰ १९, THE NUMBER THE MARGIN ABOVE PROMISED IT WOULD TAKE — `LoadField`'s own
॰ half has arrived. It is १९ and not १८ for exactly the reason written there:
॰ `ir.rs` reserved १८ in prose, prose does not claim a kind, and १८ went to
॰ whichever half landed first, which was `LoadGlobal`.
सार्वजनिक चरः क्षेत्राज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १९ ।     ॰ Instruction::LoadField(ValueId, u64)
॰ २० — AND THIS ONE'S TWIN DID NOT EXIST ON EITHER SIDE, which is what makes
॰ it different from the two above rather than more of the same. `LoadGlobal`
॰ and `LoadField` were both already variants of `ir.rs`'s `Instruction` when
॰ their `.t1` halves arrived; the numbering argument was only ever about WHICH
॰ number. There is no index instruction in `ir.rs` at all, so this kind and
॰ `Instruction::LoadIndex` are one pair added together, and the twin table
॰ pairs them from the day both exist.
॰
॰ WHY NOT REUSE `क्षेत्राज्ञाभेद` WITH A ZERO OFFSET, which would have worked and
॰ cost nothing: `Add(base, Mul(index, width))` is an address and a field load
॰ at offset ० reads it, so no new kind, no emitter arm and no decode entry.
॰ Refused on the argument the arm at `क्षेत्र` makes for its own shape number —
॰ a reused kind adds every INDEX read to the FIELD count in silence, and a
॰ census that cannot separate them is wrong permanently in exchange for a
॰ smaller diff once.
॰
॰ THE OFFSET IS DYNAMIC AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON A NEW KIND IS NEEDED.
॰ `LoadField` carries its offset as a `u64` decided at build time; an index is
॰ a VALUE, so this kind carries two मूल्याङ्क and the scaling by the element's
॰ width is built as instructions rather than folded into a constant.
सार्वजनिक चरः सूच्याज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २० ।      ॰ Instruction::LoadIndex(ValueId, ValueId, u64) — `W-294`: the third is the element width in OCTETS, carried in ध्रुवमूल्यम्

॰ ══════════ २१–२३ — AN ADDRESS IS A VALUE (`research/28`, RULED 2026-09-11) ══
॰ THE THREE KINDS ABOVE DIFFER ONLY IN HOW AN ADDRESS IS FORMED, and each then
॰ does one load. `क्षेत्र` is base+CONSTANT, `सूची` is base+RUNTIME, `वैश्विक` is a
॰ PC-relative LABEL — and all three end in `आहारः`. Completing the grid the
॰ obvious way wants EIGHT kinds: three address forms times two directions, the
॰ load/store invariant and only the arithmetic varying.
॰
॰ THAT SMALL DIFFERENCE IS THE MEASUREMENT AND NOT THE CONVENIENCE. `W-283`
॰ built `StoreGlobal` end to end and reported the backend as "two lines per
॰ kind — each store is its load's address computation plus `निधानम्`". A
॰ difference that small between two kinds means the kinds are not the right
॰ unit. The owner ruled on that evidence: form the address as a VALUE, then
॰ load or store AT it. Five kinds replace eight and writes stop being a
॰ separate design from reads.
॰
॰ IT WAS ALREADY LATENT HERE. `सूची` emits `योगः rd, base, off` and then loads
॰ from `rd` — an address in a register, built and consumed inside one kind.
॰ These three make that step nameable instead of hidden.
॰
॰ THE CENSUS KEEPS ITS RESOLUTION, which is the trap in the obvious version of
॰ this refactor. `field_base_not_a_name`, `index_declined` and the
॰ `name_global_*` causes are all statements about address FORMATION, so they
॰ stay separable precisely because the three `स्थान` kinds stay distinct. One
॰ undifferentiated `LoadAt` would have destroyed that permanently — the same
॰ argument the `सूची` margin above makes against reusing `क्षेत्र` at offset ०.
॰
॰ COST, RULED AND ACCEPTED: nothing here distinguishes an address from an
॰ integer, so the typechecker must stop them interchanging. Not yet built.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकस्थानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २१ । ॰ Instruction::AddrOfGlobal(SymbolId)

॰ २२ — `आहारः <dest> <addr>त् ०`. ONE line, because the address arrived built.
॰ The base is अपादान: the place read FROM.
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानाहाराज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २२ ।  ॰ Instruction::LoadAt(ValueId)

॰ २३ — `निधानम् <addr>य् ० <src>`. THE BASE CHANGES ITS KARAKA AND IT IS NOT
॰ COSMETIC: the load's base is `त्` (अपादान, read from), the store's is `य्`
॰ (अधिकरण, written to). A store written by copying the load's roles is refused
॰ by the assembler — `स्थिर० and स्थिर२ both claim अपादान`. Loud, and paid once.
॰
॰ THE SILENT ONE IS ELSEWHERE AND IT IS THE REASON THIS KIND SHIPS WITH A
॰ SURVIVAL TEST RATHER THAN AN EMISSION TEST. `ir.rs`'s `is_side_effecting()`
॰ matched only `Call` and `Store`; a store kind missing from it is deleted as
॰ dead code with NO diagnostic — the program compiles, assembles, runs, and
॰ drops every write. Asserting that a write EMITS cannot catch it. The
॰ assertion has to be that a write SURVIVES OPTIMISATION.
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थाननिधानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २३ । ॰ Instruction::StoreAt(ValueId, ValueId)

॰ ══════════ २४–२६ — THE STORAGE, AND ADDRESSES INTO IT (`W-284`) ══════════
॰ २१–२३ above form an address from a LABEL and spend it. These three complete
॰ the model: २४ MAKES the storage a record lives in, and २५/२६ form addresses
॰ into it, which २२/२३ then spend exactly as they spend २१'s.
॰
॰ NUMBERS READ OFF THIS FILE AT THE MOMENT THESE LINES WERE WRITTEN, not taken
॰ from a plan. Kinds are claimed by DECLARATION here, in landing order, and must
॰ stay contiguous १..=N because `the_kind_table_scan_is_not_vacuous` refuses a
॰ hole. An allocation in a message is a plan; the number in this file is the
॰ fact — and an earlier row's `निक्षेपक्षेत्राज्ञाभेद` २१, written against a tree
॰ where २१ was free, is exactly what that rule is for. That kind is not ported:
॰ a field write is २५ then २३, so `StoreField` is not a kind this model has.

॰ २४ — A RECORD ALLOCATION, and it exists because THE TWO HALVES DISAGREED
॰ about what `भवति ०` means for a record type: `nirvahana.rs`'s `zero_at`
॰ answers `Value::Record` with every field zeroed, while `ir.rs` had no record
॰ concept at all and lowered it to `ConstInt(0)` — A NULL POINTER. The corpus's
॰ construction idiom is `चरः नव ॱॱ आज्ञा भवति ० ।` followed by field writes, so
॰ the compiled half was building every record at address zero and only never
॰ noticed because the field write was STUBBED and therefore a no-op. Lowering
॰ the write made it observable: `artha.t1` and `ir.t1` faulted at `addr: 0`.
॰ THAT IS WHY THIS KIND AND २५ LAND TOGETHER — either alone is a defect.
॰
॰ SIZE IS `८ × field count`, the owner's ruling: a record is BY REFERENCE, one
॰ word per field, so a field's offset is `WORD × declaration index` and the size
॰ is `WORD × count`. THE INTERPRETER DOES NOT CHANGE — the two halves are meant
॰ to describe a record differently, and this kind is the compiled half finally
॰ describing it at all.
॰
॰ A STATIC BUMP REGION, NOT A FRAME, DECIDED BY MEASUREMENT: 38 corpus routines
॰ RETURN a struct type, so a record built in a frame dangles in every one.
सार्वजनिक चरः रचनाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २४ ।       ॰ Instruction::AllocRecord(u64)

॰ २५ — `योगः <dest> <base>न <offset>न`. The field READ १९ with its load
॰ removed, exactly as २१ is the global read १८ with its load removed. The
॰ offset is a BUILD-TIME CONSTANT in `ध्रुवमूल्यम्`, never `स्थानक्रम`: a local's
॰ slot is a frame index and gets scaled and spill-adjusted; a field's offset is
॰ already a byte count against a runtime base and must meet neither.
॰ IT BEARS NO LOCAL. It addresses a record, not the frame, so the frame-sizing
॰ pass must not see it — and it does not, because that pass reads `स्थानक्रम`
॰ only for the आहार and निधान kinds.
सार्वजनिक चरः क्षेत्रस्थानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २५ । ॰ Instruction::AddrOfField(ValueId, u64)

॰ २६ — `योगः <dest> <base>न <index>न`. BOTH operands are values, where २५ takes
॰ a value and a constant — the same asymmetry as १९ against २०, and a decoder
॰ reading `ध्रुवमूल्यम्` for this kind's second operand makes every index address
॰ offset zero IN SILENCE.
॰
॰ THE INDEX ARRIVES ALREADY SCALED, by the builder below, exactly as २०'s does.
॰ Scaling in the emitter as well would multiply twice and address past the end
॰ of every record but the first — and a doubled stride is a legal address, so
॰ nothing would say so. The two sides must agree about who scales; it is the
॰ builder, and this line is where that is written down.
सार्वजनिक चरः सूचीस्थानाज्ञाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २६ ।  ॰ Instruction::AddrOfIndex(ValueId, ValueId)

॰ enum CmpOp — the six branch conditions of ADR-0008, in that ADR's order.
॰ The grammar's five `compare_op`s lower to four of them — समम् असमम् न्यूनम्
॰ बृहत्समम् — and `अधिकम्` is न्यून with its operands exchanged; the SIGNED
॰ pair is chosen because the reference interpreter compares signed numbers
॰ (`nirvahana.rs`, `binop`). The unsigned two are declared so the six are six
॰ and built by nothing until a type reaches this builder.
सार्वजनिक चरः समतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।          ॰ CmpOp::Eq  — समलङ्घनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः विषमतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।        ॰ CmpOp::Ne  — विषमलङ्घनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः न्यूनतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।       ॰ CmpOp::Lt  — न्यूनलङ्घनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्यूनतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।      ॰ CmpOp::Ge  — अन्यूनलङ्घनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः अचिह्नन्यूनतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।  ॰ CmpOp::Ltu — अचिह्नन्यूनलङ्घनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः अचिह्नान्यूनतुलनाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ । ॰ CmpOp::Geu — अचिह्नान्यूनलङ्घनम्


॰ ══════════════════ terminator kinds ══════════════════
॰ ir.rs has exactly FOUR, and the fourth is `W-198`'s. The transliterated
॰ file this replaces declared a conditional branch, कओनडबअरआंच, when NO
॰ Rust source in the tree had one — evidence that it was not transliterated
॰ from ir.rs at all. The one declared below is different in kind: it was
॰ added to `ir.rs` and here in the SAME commit, as the one terminator a
॰ language with `यदि` and `यावत्` cannot lower without (research/22 §4.3 —
॰ Return and Branch express call-and-return, not a marker returning into
॰ its own run), so the twins stay twins. It is ४ and not ३ because both
॰ twins already had THREE terminators, not the two the `W-198` row counted:
॰ `अगम्यावसानभेद` was here, declared and built by nothing.
॰
॰ Rule X3, which the arms below keep: a शाखावसान's two targets lie inside
॰ the enclosing span, a back-edge targets a point inside its own span, and
॰ there is NO jump-to-anywhere.

सार्वजनिक चरः प्रत्यागमनावसानभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।  ॰ Terminator::Return(Option<ValueId>)
सार्वजनिक चरः लङ्घनावसानभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।      ॰ Terminator::Branch(BlockId)
सार्वजनिक चरः अगम्यावसानभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।      ॰ Terminator::Unreachable
सार्वजनिक चरः शाखावसानभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।       ॰ Terminator::CondBranch(ValueId, BlockId, BlockId)


॰ ══════════════════ the two identifiers ══════════════════
॰ ValueId(pub usize) and BlockId(pub usize) are newtypes over an index.
॰ T1 has no tuple struct, so each is a one-field संरचना — the same move
॰ सङ्केतन makes for the (u32, u32) pair it calls अंशयुग्म. They are named
॰ types rather than bare न६४ because a value number and a block number are
॰ counted by different counters and are never interchangeable.

सार्वजनिक संरचना मूल्याङ्क आरभ्य   ॰ ValueId
    क्रमाङ्क ॱॱ न६४                 ॰ ० means none — see ON INDEX ZERO above
समाप्तम् ।

सार्वजनिक संरचना पर्वाङ्क आरभ्य    ॰ BlockId
    क्रमाङ्क ॱॱ न६४                 ॰ ० means none
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ what a function is made of ══════════════════

॰ one instruction and the value it defines — Instruction, together with the
॰ ValueId of Rust's (ValueId, Instruction) pair. The pair is FOLDED IN
॰ rather than made a second struct: T1 has no tuple, and an instruction
॰ that does not know which value it defines is unreadable to उत्सर्जन,
॰ which must map a value onto a register.
सार्वजनिक संरचना आज्ञा आरभ्य
    भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ which of the five kinds above
    फलम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क ऽ              ॰ the ValueId this instruction defines
    ध्रुवमूल्यम् ॱॱ अ६४ ऽ            ॰ ConstInt's i64
    संज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                 ॰ Call's SymbolId — the node's संज्ञासूचकाङ्क, SymbolId+१, ० = none; `W-204`
    आदानारम्भ ॱॱ न६४ ऽ              ॰ Call's arguments: first index into आदानकोश — `W-204`
    आदानसंख्यान ॱॱ न६४ ऽ            ॰ Call's arguments: how many — `W-204`
    वाम ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क ऽ               ॰ every binary kind's left operand; Store's value — `W-245`
    दक्षिण ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क ऽ            ॰ every binary kind's right operand
    प्राचलक्रम ॱॱ न६४ ऽ             ॰ Param's index into the parameter list
    उपभेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                  ॰ Cmp's CmpOp, one of the six above — `W-245`
    स्थानक्रम ॱॱ न६४ ऽ              ॰ Load's and Store's frame slot — `W-245`
    पाठारम्भ ॱॱ न६४ ऽ               ॰ ConstStr's octets: first index into पाठाक्षरकोश — `W-254`
    पाठसंख्यान ॱॱ न६४               ॰ ConstStr's octets: how many — `W-254`
समाप्तम् ।

॰ how a block ends — Terminator. भेद ० is Rust's None.
सार्वजनिक संरचना अवसान आरभ्य
    भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ ० = no terminator yet
    मूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क ऽ           ॰ Return's Option<ValueId>, ० for None; CondBranch's condition
    लक्ष्यम् ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क ऽ           ॰ Branch's BlockId; CondBranch's then-block
    अन्यलक्ष्यम् ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क         ॰ CondBranch's else-block, ० for every other kind — `W-198`
समाप्तम् ।

॰ a basic block — Block. Rust's Vec<(ValueId, Instruction)> is a contiguous
॰ run of आज्ञाकोश, because a block's instructions are appended in order and
॰ nothing between them belongs to another block.
सार्वजनिक संरचना पर्व आरभ्य
    अङ्कन ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क ऽ              ॰ id
    आज्ञारम्भ ॱॱ न६४ ऽ              ॰ insts: first index into आज्ञाकोश
    आज्ञासंख्यान ॱॱ न६४ ऽ           ॰ insts: how many
    अवसानम् ॱॱ अवसान                ॰ terminator: Option<Terminator>
समाप्तम् ।

॰ a function — Function. Rust's HashMap<BlockId, Block> is keyed on a dense
॰ counter and filled in key order, so it is an array and is stored as one.
सार्वजनिक संरचना वृत्ति आरभ्य
    नाम ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ name: SymbolId
    पर्वारम्भ ॱॱ न६४ ऽ              ॰ blocks: first index into पर्वकोश
    पर्वसंख्यान ॱॱ न६४ ऽ            ॰ blocks: how many
    प्रवेशपर्व ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क           ॰ entry_block
समाप्तम् ।


॰ ══════════════════ the builder's state ══════════════════
॰ IrBuilder's three fields. Rust holds them in a struct because a Rust
॰ builder is a value; व्याकर holds the same kind of state in module चरः,
॰ and this file follows व्याकर rather than opening a second convention.
॰ आरम्भः below is the port of IrBuilder::new and resets all of them.
॰
॰ THE LAST TWO ARE RUST'S `current_block: &mut Block` — `W-198`. Rust threads
॰ the block being filled through build_statement as a parameter; a यदि or a
॰ यावत् must CLOSE the block it was handed and open another, which a callee
॰ cannot do to a `&mut Block`. So the block in hand is module state too:
॰ which block the next appended instruction belongs to, and where that
॰ block's instructions began.

सार्वजनिक चरः अग्रिममूल्याङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।    ॰ IrBuilder::next_val
सार्वजनिक चरः अग्रिमपर्वाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ IrBuilder::next_block
सार्वजनिक चरः वृत्तिकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः वृत्ति भवति ० ।   ॰ IrBuilder::functions
सार्वजनिक चरः वृत्तिसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ IrBuilder::functions.len()
सार्वजनिक चरः पर्वकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः पर्व भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः पर्वसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ the highest block id written — see पर्वयोजनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः आज्ञाकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः आज्ञा भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः आज्ञासूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ ══════════ A CROSS-MODULE CALLEE'S MODULE AND ROUTINE ══════════
॰ `W-xmodule`. The twin of `chain.rs:666`'s third branch: a call whose callee
॰ the resolver took on trust carries `संज्ञासूचकाङ्क` ० — the resolver numbers
॰ symbols per program and a foreign routine is in no scope it holds — so
॰ `यन्त्राह्वानोत्सर्जनम्` looks up ० , finds nothing, and refuses the module with
॰ `Refusal::UnnamedSymbol`. MEASURED: `kosha.t1` refuses at emit with `भेद ४`,
॰ `symbol ०`, while `ashtaka` and `lex` emit — their calls are intra-module and
॰ resolve. Eighteen references, five callees, all nine of which `ashtaka` names.
॰
॰ THE MODULE IS IN THE AST AND NEVER IN THE RESOLVER, which is why `chain.rs`
॰ reaches for the callee NODE rather than widening a name lookup: `परिसर` holds
॰ `प्रविष्टयः` and `संज्ञाप्रविष्टि` holds `नाम` and `संज्ञा`, and neither records a
॰ module — in EITHER half, `resolve.rs`'s `Vec<HashMap<String, SymbolId>>`
॰ included. A name lookup cannot answer a question the table has no column for.
॰
॰ PUBLISHED HERE AND READ BY THE EMITTER, which is the direction that already
॰ holds — `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन` reads `मध्यरूपॱआज्ञाकोश` and this file calls nothing of
॰ its. Making `ir.t1` call `यन्त्रनामयोजनम्` is the obvious move and it would
॰ REVERSE that direction and close a cycle. The parts are stored separately
॰ because `यन्त्रनाम` stores `मण्डल` and `वृत्तिनाम` separately; a fused label here
॰ would be the one place in the emitter's name path where they are joined, and
॰ so the one place a later reader splits on the wrong separator.
सार्वजनिक चरः बाह्यमण्डलकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः बाह्यवृत्तिकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः बाह्यसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE SYNTHETIC BAND, AND IT IS DISJOINT BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY CARE.
॰ `chain.rs` reserves two: `:598` mints `1_000_000 + i` for a routine the
॰ resolver did not name, and `:606` mints from `2_000_000` for a cross-module
॰ callee. The `.t1` side already carries the first — `shrinkhala.t1:236` writes
॰ `१०००००० योगः क्रमः` for exactly that case — and the second was unused until
॰ this row: ZERO occurrences of २०००००० across every `.t1` source. The
॰ resolver's own `अग्रिमसंज्ञा` restarts at ० per program and counts up, so real
॰ symbols are small. A collision here would be invisible to every count and
॰ would show only as a call reaching the wrong routine, with both names
॰ plausible — which is why the band is stated and not assumed.
॰
॰ AND A HAZARD THAT WILL LOOK LIKE CORRECTNESS: this mint and `chain.rs:606`
॰ BOTH number from २०००००० and BOTH walk callees in source order, and BOTH now
॰ deduplicate by `(module, routine)` — so for the same module they will often
॰ produce THE SAME symbol for the same callee. That agreement is a coincidence
॰ of two independent numberings, not a shared decision, and nothing checks it.
॰
॰ THE DEDUPLICATION IS WHAT MAKES THEM AGREE AT ALL, and it was added second:
॰ before it this arm minted once per call SITE and `chain.rs` once per callee,
॰ so the two diverged for any routine called twice and the coincidence could not
॰ arise. Matching the twin's rule bought correctness in the table and, as a side
॰ effect, made a false signal possible that was not possible before. Today it is harmless because the paths are
॰ disjoint: `t1_driver.rs` seeds nothing from Rust, and the census's
॰ `write_names_into_t1` seeds everything, so the two never both fill one table.
॰ THE DAY A RUST-SEEDED STEP IS ADDED TO THE `.t1` PATH, the numbers agreeing
॰ will read as evidence the port is right. It is the twin trap one level down —
॰ not two implementations agreeing, but two COUNTERS — and a twin check cannot
॰ see it, because agreement is what it is built to reward.
सार्वजनिक चरः बाह्यसंज्ञारम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति २०००००० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वर्तमानपर्व ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क भवति ० ।    ॰ current_block's id
सार्वजनिक चरः वर्तमानारम्भाज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।  ॰ current_block's first instruction index

॰ `W-279` — DID THE STATEMENT JUST BUILT CLOSE THE BLOCK IN HAND?
॰ १ when the last thing `वाक्यरचना` emitted was a TERMINATOR — today only
॰ `प्रत्यागमनम्`, which closes the block in hand and opens a fresh one after
॰ itself. Read by the `यदि` arm, which must NOT write its join लङ्घन into a
॰ block a return has already walked away from: measured on rung 101, whose
॰ arms BOTH return, that wrote two jumps nothing reaches and left the join
॰ orphaned behind them — three dead instructions, and the ladder carried
॰ five in all (rungs 98 and 100 one each, rung 101 these three).
॰
॰ CLEARED AT THE TOP OF `वाक्यरचना`, so an arm that does not set it reports
॰ ० whatever the statement before it did, and set back to ० by the `यदि` and
॰ `यावत्` arms before they answer: both leave a LIVE block in hand (the join,
॰ the exit) however their bodies ended, and a nested return's १ leaking out
॰ through them would make the enclosing arm drop a join jump that is needed.
सार्वजनिक चरः वाक्यविरामः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ the statement just built terminated

॰ THE FOURTH ARENA — `W-204`. Rust's Call carries a Vec<ValueId>; an आज्ञा
॰ carries a first index and a count into this, so every call's arguments are
॰ one contiguous run, laid end to end in call order. Item (c) at the foot of
॰ this file waited on it.
सार्वजनिक चरः आदानकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः मूल्याङ्क भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः आदानसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ `W-254` — EVERY STRING LITERAL'S OCTETS, one contiguous run each, laid end to
॰ end in the order the literals are lowered. `पाठारम्भ` and `पाठसंख्यान` on the
॰ instruction are a run in here, exactly as `आदानारम्भ` and `आदानसंख्यान` are a
॰ run in आदानकोश.
॰
॰ WHY THE OCTETS ARE COPIED HERE RATHER THAN POINTED AT IN THE SOURCE. A
॰ literal's value is ALMOST a contiguous span of the line it is written on —
॰ `lex.rs`'s `string_value` copies `line[start..end]` and keeps interior
॰ whitespace to the octet — but ADR-0011's doubling breaks that: in
॰ `उक्तम् इति इति इति` the value is the single word `इति`, and the source span
॰ holds two. The reference copies through the first `इति` and resumes after the
॰ second, so a value is a CONCATENATION of spans and not one span. The corpus
॰ uses this: nineteen sites across five files. A pair of offsets into the source
॰ could not express it, so the octets are built here.
सार्वजनिक चरः पाठाक्षरकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः पाठाक्षरसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE SCRATCH STACK BEHIND IT. A run must be CONTIGUOUS, and an argument may
॰ itself be a call: `ग आरभ्य ३ ऽ ग आरभ्य ४ समाप्तम् समाप्तम्` lowers the inner
॰ call — and appends ITS run — between the outer call's first and second
॰ argument. Appending each argument's value to आदानकोश as it is built would
॰ interleave the two runs. So a call's argument values are pushed HERE as
॰ they are built, in written order, and moved to आदानकोश in one piece once
॰ the last one exists. Nested calls push and pop their own entries before
॰ the enclosing call pushes its next, so the stack balances by construction.
सार्वजनिक चरः आदानसञ्चयकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः मूल्याङ्क भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE FIRST REFUSAL — `W-204`, the shape `अर्थ` gives `अनिर्णीतमस्ति`, guard
॰ included: the first refusal is the cause, the last is only where the walk
॰ ended. A call whose callee carries no symbol is refused BEFORE any
॰ instruction for it is appended, and `कार्यक्रमरचना` then answers ०. The
॰ token index is the callee's name token when it has one — a reader turns it
॰ into a line through पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश — and ० when the callee is not a name.
सार्वजनिक चरः अनिर्णीताह्वानमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अनिर्णीताह्वानचिह्नकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ TWO SIDE TABLES FOR THE EMITTER'S CENSUS — `W-237`, research/25 §4. Neither
॰ is a field of आज्ञा or वृत्ति, because neither has a twin in ir.rs: Rust's
॰ resolver holds every module, so its `Call(SymbolId, ..)` and `Function.name`
॰ already say WHICH routine; here the resolver takes a qualified member on
॰ trust (संज्ञा ० — the आह्वान arm's own exception) and `कार्यक्रमरचना` writes
॰ ० for every routine's नाम. A census that must LABEL a routine and NAME the
॰ callee of a cross-module call therefore reads these, indexed like the arenas
॰ they shadow: आह्वेयकोश by instruction index (the callee NODE of a Call —
॰ a वास्तु index; ० when the instruction is not a call or the callee is not a
॰ name or field), वृत्तिनामचिह्नककोश by routine index (the declaration's NAME
॰ TOKEN, `व्याकर ॱ घोषणा ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क`). `W-223` — the shared declaration
॰ space — is what makes the first redundant; the second goes when नाम is
॰ written from the resolver's symbol.
सार्वजनिक चरः आह्वेयकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वृत्तिनामचिह्नककोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE LOCALS OF THE ROUTINE IN HAND — `W-245`. A slot per name, parameters
॰ first in declaration order, then every `चरः` as the body reaches it; the
॰ slot number is the index here minus one. Keyed by the name's TOKEN, and
॰ looked up by TEXT, because a `चर` statement carries its name token and no
॰ symbol (the resolver declares it in a scope that is closed by the time this
॰ builder runs), and a use carries a symbol and no slot. A name redeclared in
॰ a sibling block takes the slot it already has. ir.rs's twin is the
॰ `locals: HashMap<String, usize>` its `Function` would hold.
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानीयचिह्नककोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानीयसंख्यान ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE STUB CENSUS — `W-245`, research/25 §4's `zero_constants` split by cause.
॰ Every ध्रुवाज्ञा the catch-all below writes for a shape it does not lower
॰ records WHY, by instruction index (० = a real instruction), and every stub —
॰ an expression's or a statement's — counts once under its cause here, so the
॰ encode census can print `paradigm_ir_stub_<cause> N` by name and a reader can
॰ see which shape to lower next. The causes, numbered:
॰   १ नाम with no symbol         २ नाम of a type           ३ नाम of a device
॰   ४ नाम of a module-level चरः  ५ नाम of an import        ६ नाम of a गणना
॰   ७ नाम of a local this table does not hold (declared after its use)
॰   ८ उक्त (a string literal)    ९ सूचकाङ्क (an index)     १० क्षेत्र (a field)
॰   ११ शून्यम्                    १२ समावेश (an embed)      १३ खण्ड (a slice)
॰   १४ आह्वान whose callee is an index (W-228's slice-as-call)
॰   १५ any other expression kind
॰   २० सम to a field  २१ सम to an index  २२ सम to a name that is no local  २३ सम to another shape
॰   २७ सूचकाङ्क this arm declines — the index lowering's residue, and NOT the
॰      same statement as ९. ९ meant "no index is lowered at all"; २६ means the
॰      arm ran, walked the base's type, and refused THIS one. Split when it is
॰      reported: an element width this arm does not emit a load for is MY
॰      implementation declining, where a base whose type the arenas cannot
॰      reach is the corpus, and only the first is a scope decision.
॰   ४५ क्षेत्र whose base's RECORDED TYPE IS THE CHECKER'S POISON — not a
॰      corpus fact and not a shape this file declines, but `अर्थ` never having
॰      typed the declaration. 359 where cause ३२ read 399 on `ir,encode`, and
॰      ३२'s residue is the ४१ that must still refuse; see the table at the raise.
सार्वजनिक चरः अपूर्णहेतुकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः अपूर्णगणनाकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ EXCLUSIVE, AND ४५ BECAUSE OF IT (2026-09-18). `सीमा` is read both ways in
॰ this corpus — 58 loops are bounded by one — and on 2026-09-17 the word caused
॰ two silent defects in 24 hours: `खण्डपाठः` handed a LENGTH where it wanted a
॰ bound, and `अपूर्णयोगः` reading this bound as exclusive when the reset treated
॰ it as inclusive, so cause ४४ was never counted at all.
॰
॰ THE RULING IS EXCLUSIVE: a `सीमा` is the first value NOT in the table. That is
॰ the majority reading here and the one that agrees with the rest of the
॰ vocabulary — `आरम्भः` and `दैर्घ्यम्` disagree because one is absolute and one
॰ relative, and `< सीमा` sits with `दैर्घ्यम्` as a count you stop below.
॰
॰ SO THE CONSTANT MOVED AND THE LOOPS DID NOT HAVE TO. It was ४४ with cause ४४
॰ live, which IS an inclusive bound, and both loops carried `योगः १` to reach it.
॰ At ४५ every loop is plain `न्यूनम् सीमा` and clears or sums १..४४ exactly as
॰ before — IDENTICAL BEHAVIOUR, one fewer idiom, and the constant now states its
॰ own convention instead of the loops restating it twice.
॰
॰ The earlier repair made the SUM match the RESET by adding `योगः १` to it —
॰ arithmetically right, idiomatically wrong: it fitted the loop to a
॰ non-conforming constant instead of fixing the constant.
॰
॰ ४५ -> ४६ ON 2026-09-27 (`W-283`), AND THE CONVENTION IS UNTOUCHED: cause ४५
॰ (`field_qualified_type_is_poison`) is live, so the first value NOT a cause is
॰ ४६ and both loops stay plain `न्यूनम् सीमा`, clearing and summing १..४५. The
॰ paragraph above is kept as written because it is the reasoning that made the
॰ constant state its own convention; only the number moved.
सार्वजनिक चरः अपूर्णहेतुसीमा ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४६ ।


॰ WHICH OF CAUSE २७'S FIFTEEN SITES DECLINED — `W-301`, 2026-09-18.
॰
॰ Cause २७ `index_declined` is raised at FIFTEEN sites and every one of them writes
॰ the same number, so `अपूर्णगणनाकोश अङ्कः २७` says how often the index arm refused
॰ and never which check did it. Measured 2026-09-18: those fifteen are the corpus's
॰ whole cause-२७ surface and they all sit in `अभिव्यञ्जकरचना`. They are not one
॰ defect — a missing index expression, a base index past the arena, a nil base, a
॰ qualified name denoting a MODULE (which has no run to index), a base with no
॰ symbol, a type index of ०, a type arena too short, a nil type. Nine different
॰ failures under one label cannot be worked down in any order but blind.
॰
॰ THE CAUSE NUMBER IS NOT SPLIT, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. `81c2ccc7` met the same
॰ problem in `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन` — "the UnnamedSymbol refusal must name WHICH of its
॰ five sites" — and answered it by NAMING THE SITE beside the unchanged cause.
॰ Splitting २७ into fifteen causes would move `अपूर्णहेतुसीमा` — which `1cc531bd`
॰ has just re-founded as EXCLUSIVE — renumber a space
॰ that `tools/sassembly-model.py`'s `STUB_CAUSES` and `corpus-shapes.py` both pin,
॰ and still not say which site fired for the other thirty raises. A site channel does.
॰
॰ AND CAUSE ३२'S SPLIT ON 2026-09-27 DID MOVE THE BOUND, WHICH IS NOT THIS RULING
॰ BEING OVERTURNED. This channel is keyed by `स्थलाङ्कः` ALONE — `अपूर्णध्रुवस्थाने`
॰ writes `अपूर्णस्थानगणनाकोश अङ्कः स्थलाङ्कः`, with no cause in the key — so it belongs
॰ to cause २७ by construction and `t1_cause27_sites.rs` reads it as cause २७'s. A
॰ second population in it would not be a second channel; it would corrupt the first.
॰ The other half of the ruling stands and was followed: ONE cause was added, not
॰ eleven, because one kind carried 92% of the population and the rest are the residue
॰ the unsplit number is still honest about.
सार्वजनिक चरः अपूर्णस्थानगणनाकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ EXCLUSIVE, per the ruling above: १६ is the first value NOT a site, and the
॰ sites are १..१५. This constant states its own convention so no loop has to.
सार्वजनिक चरः अपूर्णस्थानसीमा ॱॱ न६४ भवति १६ ।
॰ RUN EQUALITY IS CONTENT EQUALITY (2026-09-13). `समम्` on two runs compiled to a word
॰ compare of two pointers where the interpreter compares octets — the parser's 34
॰ keyword matches were all false natively and it answered 0 declarations. It is
॰ lowered INLINE (खण्डसाम्यरचना below): a call into another module cannot be the
॰ lowering of an operator — a single-source image of ashtaka.t1 could not link.
॰ A SLICE IS A FRESH BLOCK, inline (खण्डखण्डरचना); forty-four sites.
॰ THE RECORD CURSOR, addressed from the IR (2026-09-13): the emitters own the label
॰ `रचनासूचकः` (module-less, so the pair ("", "रचनासूचकः") spells it); run growth
॰ bumps it with LoadAt/StoreAt through वैश्विकस्थानाज्ञाभेद — no new kind.
सार्वजनिक चरः रचनासूचकसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति १००००००३ ।
॰ The cursor holds an OFFSET into `रचनाक्षेत्रम्` (the allocator answers region +
॰ offset); the region's label is the pair ("", "रचनाक्षेत्रम्").
सार्वजनिक चरः रचनाक्षेत्रसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति १००००००४ ।
॰
॰ ॥ DO NOT INSTRUMENT THESE BY INJECTING INTO AN EMITTER ॥ 2026-09-19.
॰
॰ These two labels are the obvious place to reach when someone wants the
॰ allocator's trajectory out of a running image, and the obvious method — have
॰ the back end append `la`/`ld` and a print at each trace point — BREAKS THE
॰ ORACLE IT WOULD BE DEBUGGING. There are TWO emitters, `riscv64.rs` and
॰ `yantrotsarjana.t1`, and they are compared octet for octet (`tools/demo.sh`
॰ prints TWINS AGREE with the count). Injecting into one makes them disagree on
॰ every routine. Injecting into both identically restores agreement and leaves
॰ the twin check unable to catch a divergence IN THE INJECTED CODE, which is
॰ the code being trusted.
॰
॰ TWO THINGS ABOUT THE VALUES, so the next reader does not rediscover them:
॰ the cursor holds an OFFSET and not an address, so subtracting the region base
॰ is double-counting; and the only output is `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्`, ONE OCTET, so a
॰ 64-bit value is eight calls or a hex writer, never one print.
॰
॰ THE SHAPE THAT WOULD WORK is an intercepted intrinsic, the way
॰ `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्` already is: collected into the interpreter's sink on one side
॰ and lowered to a store on the other, written as one pair so the halves cannot
॰ drift. Nothing reserves a name for it here — a declaration with no mechanism
॰ behind it reads as a capability, and this is a design note, not a promise.
॰
॰ AND IT WAS NOT NEEDED. The fault this was proposed for was localised by
॰ diffing the octet traces both engines ALREADY write — 292 records agreeing,
॰ then 374, then 586 identical — plus a disassembly of the faulting pc. The
॰ cheapest instrument remains printing a value the program already computes.
॰ ॥ THE RUN HEADER ॥ (2026-09-13) two words before the base: capacity in OCTETS at
॰ base − १६, length in ELEMENTS at base − ८. A string literal's capacity word is ०
॰ (its first write copies it to the heap — the interpreter's copy-on-write); an
॰ arena's is its zero padding word (same); a heap block's is what was allocated.
सार्वजनिक चरः खण्डशीर्षविस्तार ॱॱ न६४ भवति १६ ।
॰ ONE GROWTH ROUTINE PER MODULE (2026-09-13): the growth sequence inline at every index
॰ store tripled the lowering's work (61.7M → 175.6M steps on ashtaka alone). It is now
॰ synthesised once per module that needs it — `खण्डवृद्धिः`, three parameters (base, index,
॰ element width), answers the base after growth and the length bump — and a site pushes
॰ three arguments and calls. The driver names the symbol as (module, "खण्डवृद्धिः").
सार्वजनिक चरः वृद्धिवृत्तिसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति १००००००५ ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वृद्धिवृत्तिप्रयुक्तम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
॰ ४३ -> ४४ WITH cause ४४ `name_global_declsite_zero`, in the same edit that adds
॰ it — and the discipline failed once before it held. The edit was written, gated
॰ and COMMITTED with the raise at ४४ and this line still reading ४३. The commit
॰ message even argued a bound question and answered it for the WRONG TABLE:
॰ `रचितशेषसीमा` below bounds SHAPE numbers and correctly does not move, which is
॰ true, irrelevant, and reads exactly like having checked. ASKING THE RIGHT
॰ QUESTION OF THE WRONG TABLE LOOKS IDENTICAL TO HAVING ASKED IT.
॰ २५ -> २६ WITH cause २६ `field_base_not_a_name`, in the same edit that adds it.
॰ २४ -> २५ WITH cause २५ `field_qualified`, in the same edit that adds it, which
॰ is the whole discipline this margin exists to enforce.
॰ २६ -> २७ WITH cause २७ `index_declined`, same edit, same discipline. २६ is
॰ `field_base_not_a_name` and LANDED FIRST, so the run is २५ २६ २७ with no hole
॰ after all — but the margin that expected one stands, because causes ARE a
॰ sparse map (१६..१९ are unused) and the next lane should not tidy a gap. It is the instruction KINDS that must be contiguous १..=N, which
॰ `the_kind_table_scan_is_not_vacuous` refuses a gap in.
॰ THIS IS A RESET BOUND AS WELL AS A CEILING, exactly as `रचितशेषसीमा` below says of
॰ itself: `आरम्भः` clears १..अपूर्णहेतुसीमा, and the arena is sized by what that reset
॰ writes. So a cause numbered ABOVE this line does not merely go uncounted — it indexes
॰ one past the end and FAULTS, `entry 24 is outside an arena of 24`, raised at the read
॰ and naming nothing about the cause that was added. RAISE THIS IN THE SAME EDIT THAT
॰ ADDS A CAUSE. W-278 added cause २४, read only the twin's margin, and walked into the
॰ trap this file already described.
॰
॰ ॥ AND THE SENTENCE THAT USED TO STAND HERE WAS FALSE ॥ `W-264`. It claimed the
॰ imperative "is on both bounds now". It never was: `रचितशेषसीमा` below carries the
॰ reset-bound argument and not this instruction, and a grep for the imperative finds
॰ exactly one. A margin asserting a duplication that does not exist is worse than no
॰ margin, because it is precisely what stops the next reader checking — which is how
॰ this trap was walked into a fifth time, by the author of the warning, in this file,
॰ minutes after writing it.
॰
॰ SO THE PROSE NO LONGER CARRIES IT. `each_arena_bound_equals_the_highest_entry_of_the
॰ _table_it_bounds` in `t1_transcriptions.rs` DERIVES both bounds from this file and
॰ both tables from `paradigm_encode.rs` and refuses either direction by name. An
॰ instruction repeated in two margins is a convention; a bound checked against its own
॰ table is a guard, and only one of the two survives an author in a hurry.

॰ AND ITS OTHER HALF: what the builder LOWERED, by shape, so the census can
॰ say how many stubs each arm of `W-245` retired — before that row every one
॰ of these sites was a stub, so "before" is this count plus the stub count
॰ above. The shapes, numbered:
॰   १ a parameter (Param + Store)   २ a local read (Load)   ३ a `चरः` (Store)
॰   ४ a `सम` to a local (Store)     ५ a बूल literal          ६ `ऋण` (unary)
॰   १०+k the operator of `वास्तु`'s kind k (१०+१ योग … १०+१५ बृहत्सम)
॰ ॥ THE MODULE'S OWN GLOBALS — `W-278` ॥
॰ One entry per module-level `चरः` this source declares: the symbol it was
॰ minted under, and the word its initialiser gives. `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन` emits one
॰ labelled, EXPORTED quad per entry, and every module that reads the global
॰ reaches that one object through the linker.
॰ THE DECLARING MODULE EMITS IT AND NOBODY ELSE: a copy per module would take a
॰ cross-module write in one and the read from another, so a shared global would
॰ answer its initialiser for ever.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकमण्डलकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकनामकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकमूल्यकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४ भवति ० ।
॰ ॥ वैश्विकसामर्थ्यकोश ॥ HOW MANY OCTETS THE EMITTER RESERVES FOR THIS GLOBAL.
॰
॰ `८` for a scalar, which is exactly what the three arenas above have always
॰ described: one labelled quad holding an initialiser. `खण्डसामर्थ्यम् गुणनम् ८`
॰ for a run, which is what `:2449` has given a LOCAL run since `W-287`.
॰
॰ AN OCTET COUNT AND NOT A FLAG, and the choice buys a future rather than a line.
॰ Every size in this file is already computed in octets — `खण्डसामर्थ्यम् गुणनम् ८`
॰ for a run, `क्षेत्रसंख्या गुणनम् ८` for a record — so a count speaks the
॰ vocabulary the local arm speaks, a scalar's `८` is today's behaviour rather than
॰ an exception to it, and a global RECORD comes free. A bool would answer "is it a
॰ run" and a record needs `क्षेत्रसंख्या गुणनम् ८`, so it would need a second bool
॰ or a kind. If the capacity ever becomes per-declaration, no reader changes.
॰
॰ W-287 FIXED THIS MECHANISM FOR LOCALS AND ITS FIX STOPPED AT THE ROUTINE
॰ BOUNDARY. `:701` says "a run declared `भवति ०` had no storage", which reads as a
॰ statement about runs and is a statement about runs declared INSIDE A ROUTINE. A
॰ module-level `सार्वजनिक चरः` was never reached, and **the margin recording that
॰ fix is what made the gap invisible — nobody re-asks a question a margin appears
॰ to have answered.** Whoever fixes a construct next should ask where else it
॰ appears before writing the sentence that closes it.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकसामर्थ्यकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ NOT `वैश्विकसूचकाङ्क`: `वाक्यविभाग` already declares that name, and a global is
॰ keyed by its BARE name (`W-249`), so the two would share one slot and the last
॰ module loaded would initialise it for both. Caught by
॰ `the_loader_gives_the_same_program_under_every_order_of_the_fifteen_sources`,
॰ which counts these collisions and refused a ninth.
सार्वजनिक चरः वैश्विकसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

सार्वजनिक चरः रचितगणनाकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ `W-278` raised this from २५ to २६ for `global_load`. IT IS THE RESET BOUND
॰ AS WELL AS THE CEILING: `रचितारम्भः` clears १..रचितशेषसीमा between programs, so
॰ a shape counted above the bound would never be cleared and would accumulate
॰ across every source in one interpreter — the census reading a sum where it
॰ meant a count.
॰ `W-283`: २८ -> २९ IN THE SAME EDIT AS THE SHAPE THAT NEEDS IT.
॰
॰ THIS BOUND SIZES THE ARENA — `:625-629` resets `रचितगणनाकोश` by walking
॰ `१..=रचितशेषसीमा`, and that loop is the only thing that grows it. So a shape
॰ raised above the bound does NOT read back quietly: it faults on the WRITE and
॰ takes the source's IR build with it.
॰
॰ MEASURED, because this paragraph first claimed the opposite. Left at २८ with
॰ `रचितगणनम् २९` in place: `outside an arena of 29` fifteen times,
॰ `paradigm_ir_stubs` 113 against 3038, two sources assembled against fifteen.
॰ **The bound case is the LOUD one.** The quiet failure is a row declared in
॰ `LOWERED_SHAPES` that nothing ever raises — no fault, every other figure
॰ plausible, and the row simply absent.
॰
॰ Both are caught by `REQUIRED_LOWERED_SHAPES` in `paradigm_encode.rs`, which
॰ did not exist until `W-283` wrote it: the shape table was REPORTED and never
॰ CHECKED, so the control for this had no assertion to fire.
॰ `W-284`: २९ -> ३२ WITH shapes ३० `record_alloc`, ३१ `assign_field` and ३२
॰ `assign_index`, IN THE SAME EDIT THAT ADDS THEM — and the rule is written
॰ here because this fault has been met three times on this project: `entry N is
॰ outside an arena of N`, on `अपूर्णहेतुसीमा` in W-278, on this bound for a field
॰ store, and again after that. The guard
॰ `each_arena_bound_equals_the_highest_entry_of_the_table_it_bounds` catches it
॰ AT THE TABLE, but only once the table entry exists. ADD THE TABLE ENTRY AND
॰ RAISE THE BOUND IN ONE EDIT, and let the guard check the pair.
॰ `W-306`: ३४ -> ३५ WITH shape ३५ `assign_index_grown`, in the same edit that
॰ adds it at `:4729` — the growth branch of the index-assignment arm, which
॰ lowered an address and counted nothing. THE PAIR IS THE POINT: the entry loop
॰ clears `१..=रचितशेषसीमा` and that loop is the only thing sizing `रचितगणनाकोश`,
॰ so ३५ raised against a bound of ३४ does not read as an unreached arm — it
॰ indexes one past the end and the IR build DIES with `entry 35 is outside an
॰ arena of 34`. Headroom is ० again after this line, as it was before it.
सार्वजनिक चरः रचितशेषसीमा ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३५ ।     ॰ the highest shape number
॰ ३३ -> ३४ WITH shape ३४, in the same edit that adds it — `W-len`'s run-length
॰ load. THIS IS A RESET BOUND AS WELL AS A CEILING: the entry loop clears
॰ `१..=रचितशेषसीमा` and that loop is the only thing sizing `रचितगणनाकोश`, so a
॰ shape numbered above this line does not go uncounted — it indexes one past the
॰ end and the run DIES on the READ with `entry N is outside an arena of N`.
॰ Headroom was ० before this edit; the next shape pays the same attention.
॰
॰ THE BUMP'S TEN INSTRUCTIONS CARRY NO SHAPE, DELIBERATELY. They are part of the
॰ indexed-store shape ३२ rather than a lowering of their own, and minting a
॰ number for them would cost a second bound rise for bookkeeping with nothing
॰ lowered behind it. The same choice as part १'s allocation header.
॰ २६ -> २७ WITH shape २७ `field_load`, same edit, same reason as its twin above.
॰ २७ -> २८ WITH shape २८ `index_load`, same edit again. A NEW NUMBER AND NOT
॰ २७: an index read scaled and loaded is not a field read, and shape २७'s own
॰ margin gives the argument — a reused shape adds one population to another's
॰ count in silence, and a census that mixed `field` with `index` could never be
॰ un-mixed afterwards.

॰ ॥ संरचनानामघोषणा ॥ A TYPE NAME'S TOKEN -> the `व्याकर` declaration index of
॰ the `संरचना` that names it, or ० if none does. `W-279`.
॰
॰ WHY BY NAME AND NOT BY SYMBOL, WHICH I TRIED FIRST AND MEASURED WRONG: a TYPE
॰ name node carries NO symbol. `प्रकारपदम् ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क` reads ० — measured by
॰ emitting it AS AN ALLOCATION SIZE and reading the number back out of the
॰ assembly, because this file has no way to print. The resolver binds VALUE
॰ names; a type is resolved by the checker against its own tables and the AST
॰ node keeps only the token. So the declaration is found the way `अर्थ` finds
॰ it: by matching the text.
॰
॰ `प्रकारघोषणाभेद` IS २ AND A `संरचना` PRODUCES ONE. The scan is linear over the
॰ declarations, as the checker's own is; there is no name index in this file to
॰ consult and inventing one would be a row of its own.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः संरचनानामघोषणा आदाय चिह्नकाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि चिह्नकाङ्कः समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    यदि पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश ॱ दैर्घ्य न्यूनम् चिह्नकाङ्कः योगः १ आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    चरः लक्ष्यचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः चिह्नकाङ्कः अन्तः ।
    चरः लक्ष्यपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः लक्ष्यचिह्नकम् ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् व्याकरॱघोषणाकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
        चरः घोष ॱॱ व्याकरॱघोषणा भवति व्याकरॱघोषणाकोश अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः ।
        यदि घोष असमम् शून्यम् आदि
            यदि घोष ॱ भेद समम् व्याकरॱप्रकारघोषणाभेद आदि
                यदि घोष ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
                    यदि पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश ॱ दैर्घ्य अधिकम् घोष ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क आदि
                        चरः घोषचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः घोष ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
                        चरः घोषपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः घोषचिह्नकम् ।
                        यदि घोषपाठ समम् लक्ष्यपाठ आदि
                            प्रत्यागमनम् क्रमः ।
                        इति
                    इति
                इति
            इति
        इति
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

॰ ॥ आयातितसंरचनासंख्या ॥ A BARE TYPE NAME -> the field count of the `संरचना`
॰ an IMPORTED module declares under it, or ० when that is not exactly one
॰ record. `W-279`.
॰
॰ THE GAP THIS CLOSES. `संरचनानामघोषणा` scans `व्याकर`, which holds the ONE
॰ source being lowered, and the remote path beside it is gated on a MODULE
॰ PREFIX. So `चरः x ॱॱ अवकाश भवति ०` — a record of another module, spelled
॰ bare — matched neither: it fell through to `ध्रुवरचना ०`, the slot held ०,
॰ and the first field access faulted at address ० IN THE NATIVE IMAGE ONLY,
॰ because `nirvahana.rs` allocates for `भवति ०` on a record type and the
॰ interpreter never sees the defect. Eight such sites were qualified by hand on
॰ 2026-09-18 and the census (`tools/bare-type-census.py`) says the population is
॰ ०; this routine is why the ninth does not have to be found that way.
॰
॰ ॥ EXACTLY ONE, OR NOTHING — AND THIS IS THE WHOLE DESIGN ॥
॰ A bare name is NOT always resolvable. `आज्ञा` is declared public by both
॰ `मध्यरूप` and `वाक्यविभाग`, and `वाक्य` by both `वास्तु` and `वाक्यविभाग`.
॰ Answering the FIRST match would hand back a field count from the wrong
॰ record — and a wrong SIZE is worse than the null it replaces, because the
॰ null faults at the first access while a short allocation corrupts whatever
॰ was laid after it. So a tie answers ०, which leaves the site exactly as
॰ broken as it is today and no more.
॰
॰ THREE THINGS ARE REFUSED, and each is a test in
॰ `tests/w279_bare_type_lowering.rs`: a name two imported modules declare, a
॰ name only an UNIMPORTED module declares, and a declaration that is not
॰ `सार्वजनिक`. The current module's OWN entries are accepted — `वास्तु` is two
॰ FILES (ast.t1 and vastu.t1) under one module name, so a type declared in the
॰ sibling file is absent from `व्याकर` and present in the store, and it is not
॰ cross-module at all.
॰
॰ `सदस्यान्वेषणम्` CANNOT SERVE AS THE PROBE, which is why this walks the store
॰ itself: it RECORDS A REFUSAL on a miss, and a scan that asks about every
॰ candidate module would fill the diagnostic store with false ones.
॰ `मण्डलान्वेषणम्` and `आयातितम्` record nothing, which is why they are the two
॰ this calls.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः आयातितसंरचनासंख्या आदाय नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि नाम ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    ॰ THE CURRENT MODULE'S NAME, read the way the global-emitter reads it at
    ॰ `ir.t1`'s `चरघोषणाभेद` arm, and guarded the same way: an index of ० or one
    ॰ past the token cursor answers `शून्यम्`, and `चिह्नकपाठः` faults on that.
    चरः स्वमण्डलपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
    यदि व्याकरॱमण्डलनामसूचकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
        यदि व्याकरॱमण्डलनामसूचकाङ्क न्यूनम् पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
            चरः स्वमण्डलचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः व्याकरॱमण्डलनामसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
            यदि स्वमण्डलचिह्नकम् असमम् शून्यम् आदि
                स्वमण्डलपाठ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः स्वमण्डलचिह्नकम् ।
            इति
        इति
    इति
    ॰ A source with no `मण्डलम्` line imports nothing and owns nothing, so there
    ॰ is no module to resolve THROUGH and every candidate would be a guess.
    यदि स्वमण्डलपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    ॰ ॥ A PRIMITIVE IS NEVER A RECORD, AND THIS IS THE WHOLE REASON THE STORE
    ॰ WALK BELOW IS AFFORDABLE ॥ Of the 588 `चरः x ॱॱ T भवति ० ।` sites in this
    ॰ corpus, 502 are `न६४` or `अ६४` — and every one of them reaches here,
    ॰ because `संरचनानामघोषणा` answers ० for a primitive exactly as it does for
    ॰ a remote record. Without this line each of those 502 would walk the WHOLE
    ॰ declaration store of the whole corpus, which is the superlinear term the
    ॰ owner ruling of 2026-09-13 (item 3) exists to forbid adding to.
    ॰
    ॰ `मूलप्रकारार्थः` IS ASKED RATHER THAN A LIST WRITTEN HERE. It holds the
    ॰ frozen vocabulary of `spec/grammar-t1.ebnf:206-208` — the widths, the two
    ॰ floats, `बूल`, `अक्षरम्`, and both spellings of `पाठ` — and answers
    ॰ `दोषार्थभेद` for a name that is none of them. A second copy of that list
    ॰ here would drift from it silently, and `W-248` records what that costs:
    ॰ the retired `पाठः` spelling was matched in one place and not another, and
    ॰ every `ददाति पाठ` in the corpus read as poison until the mismatch was
    ॰ found.
    ॰ BOUND TO A NAME BEFORE THE FIELD IS READ, as every `ॱ` chain in this file
    ॰ is: a call is not a base this grammar lets a field hang off.
    चरः मूलार्थः ॱॱ अर्थॱअर्थप्रकार भवति अर्थॱमूलप्रकारार्थः नाम ।
    यदि मूलार्थः ॱ भेद असमम् अर्थॱदोषार्थभेद आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    ॰ ० when this source was never collected into the store; no entry carries
    ॰ module ० (the arenas are one-based), so the same-module arm below simply
    ॰ never fires and `आयातितम्` answers `असत्यम्` for an unknown module.
    चरः स्वमण्डलाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱमण्डलान्वेषणम् स्वमण्डलपाठ ।
    ॰ COUNTED, NOT SHORT-CIRCUITED: the second candidate is what makes the
    ॰ first one wrong, so the walk must finish before it may answer.
    चरः मिलितानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्षेत्रसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        यदि घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिभेदः क्रमः समम् व्याकरॱप्रकारघोषणाभेद आदि
            यदि घोषणासञ्चयॱसञ्चयपाठसाम्यम् आरभ्य घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिनाम क्रमः ऽ नाम समाप्तम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
                चरः प्रविष्टिमण्डलाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिमण्डलम् क्रमः ।
                चरः ग्राह्यम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
                यदि प्रविष्टिमण्डलाङ्कः समम् स्वमण्डलाङ्कः आदि
                    ग्राह्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                इति अन्यथा आदि
                    यदि घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिसार्वजनिकत्वम् क्रमः समम् सत्यम् आदि
                        यदि घोषणासञ्चयॱआयातितम् आरभ्य स्वमण्डलपाठ ऽ घोषणासञ्चयॱमण्डलनाम प्रविष्टिमण्डलाङ्कः समाप्तम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
                            ग्राह्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                        इति
                    इति
                इति
                यदि ग्राह्यम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
                    मिलितानि भवति मिलितानि योगः १ ।
                    यदि मिलितानि समम् १ आदि
                        क्षेत्रसंख्या भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिप्राचलसंख्या क्रमः ।
                    इति
                इति
            इति
        इति
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    यदि मिलितानि समम् १ आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् क्षेत्रसंख्या ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

॰ ॥ स्थानमात्रम् ॥ ADDRESS ONLY — the one bit that turns a read into a write.
॰ `W-284`.
॰
॰ A `क्षेत्र` or `सूचकाङ्क` target of an assignment needs EXACTLY the chain the
॰ same expression needs as a value, minus the final load. Every guard, every
॰ refusal, every cause number and the whole offset computation are shared; only
॰ the last instruction differs — `क्षेत्रस्थान` २५ where the read emits
॰ `क्षेत्र` १९, `सूचीस्थान` २६ where it emits `सूची` २०.
॰
॰ WRITING THE WALK TWICE WAS THE OBVIOUS SHAPE AND IT IS THE WRONG ONE. The
॰ field chain raises SEVENTEEN distinct causes and the index chain reads
॰ `विस्तार` and refuses a narrow element; a second copy would drift from the
॰ first silently, and the census would report two populations that had stopped
॰ meaning the same thing. A READ AND ITS WRITE MUST REFUSE THE SAME SET, and
॰ the only way to be sure of that is for there to be one set.
॰
॰ IT IS CAPTURED AND CLEARED AT THE BUILDER'S HEAD, NOT READ WHERE IT IS USED,
॰ and that is required rather than tidy: both arms lower their BASE by calling
॰ the builder recursively, and an uncleared flag would make the base an address
॰ too — `अ ॱ ब ॱ स` would store into the address of `अ ॱ ब` instead of reading
॰ it. The discipline is the one `प्रतीक्षाकोश` records in `encode.t1`: the
॰ callee clears first, "otherwise a second call inherits the first call's
॰ pendings". Here the inheritance would not fault; it would write to the wrong
॰ place and say nothing.
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थानमात्रम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।

॰ ॥ खण्डसामर्थ्यम् ॥ HOW MANY ELEMENTS A `चरः X ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः T भवति ० ।`
॰ GETS. `W-287`.
॰
॰ `W-284` made the index WRITE lower — `assign_index` २१ went 434 to zero — and
॰ every one of those writes then stored through a base of ०, because a run
॰ declared `भवति ०` had no storage. Five of nineteen corpus sources stopped at
॰ `BadAccess { addr: 8 }`, which is `० + १ × ८`: the null base plus one element.
॰ **The lowering was right and the storage was missing.**
॰
॰ A GROWABLE RUN HAS NO BUILD-TIME SIZE, SO THIS IS A CHOICE AND NOT A
॰ DERIVATION, AND BOTH OF ITS FAILURE MODES ARE STATED HERE RATHER THAN
॰ DISCOVERED:
॰   ॱ **PAST THE REGION'S END — LOUD.** The bump region is finite; an image that
॰     allocates more than `यन्त्ररचनाष्टकाः` runs off `ॱरिक्त` and faults. That
॰     is the failure this project prefers and it is the one that cannot be
॰     silent.
॰   ॱ **PAST THIS CAPACITY BUT INSIDE THE REGION — SILENT, AND IT IS THE COST.**
॰     A write to element `खण्डसामर्थ्यम्` or beyond lands in whatever the bump
॰     allocated next. Nothing refuses it. **A bounds check needs the length
॰     carried beside the pointer, which is a wider change than this one** — the
॰     allocation would gain a header word and every index would read it.
॰
॰ SO THE NUMBER IS PICKED TO MAKE THE SECOND CASE RARE RATHER THAN IMPOSSIBLE,
॰ and the honest statement is that it is a floor on correctness, not a proof of
॰ it. `१२८` words is 1 KiB per run; the region holds `५३६८७०९१२` octets (512 MiB since 2026-09-14, measured 353 MB on the first whole-corpus native compile; 320 MiB
॰ since 2026-09-13, when a full native self-compile was measured at 254 MB), so
॰ about three hundred thousand such runs per image before the loud failure.
॰
॰ ॥ AND THERE IS A HARD CEILING ON THIS CONSTANT THAT THE ASSEMBLER FOUND, NOT
॰ ME ॥ The allocation's size reaches the ISA as an `addi` immediate, which is
॰ TWELVE BITS SIGNED — `−२०४८..२०४७`. `२५६` words is exactly `२०४८` octets, one
॰ past the end, and the assembler refused with
॰
॰     instruction 10 is laid out at 0x28 but written at 0x24 — branches and
॰     names are computed from the layout, so from here the image is wrong by
॰     -4 octet(s)
॰
॰ because a size that does not fit materialises as TWO instructions in one pass
॰ and one in the other. **A layout refusal, not a wrong answer** — loud, exact,
॰ and it named the offset. `खण्डसामर्थ्यम् गुणनम् ८` MUST stay under `२०४८`
॰ until the allocation arm learns to build a wide immediate, and raising this
॰ constant past `२५५` without that change re-breaks every image that allocates
॰ a run.
सार्वजनिक चरः खण्डसामर्थ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति १२८ ।

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः रचितगणनम् आदाय रूपम् ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    रचितगणनाकोश अङ्कः रूपम् अन्तः भवति रचितगणनाकोश अङ्कः रूपम् अन्तः योगः १ ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति


॰ ══════════════════ constructing the two identifiers ══════════════════
॰ These two are the tuple-struct constructors `ValueId(n)` and `BlockId(n)`,
॰ which T1 has to spell out because it has no tuple struct to call.

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मूल्याङ्कनम् आदाय क्रमाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ददाति मूल्याङ्क आदि
    चरः नव ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ० ।
    नव ॱ क्रमाङ्क भवति क्रमाङ्क ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् नव ।
इति

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः पर्वाङ्कनम् आदाय क्रमाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ददाति पर्वाङ्क आदि
    चरः नव ॱॱ पर्वाङ्क भवति ० ।
    नव ॱ क्रमाङ्क भवति क्रमाङ्क ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् नव ।
इति


॰ ══════════════════ IrBuilder::new ══════════════════
॰ Rust returns Self with three empty fields. Here the state is the module's,
॰ so this empties it and returns nothing but ०. It must be called before a
॰ program is built, which Rust gets for free by making the builder a value.

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः आरम्भः ददाति न६४ आदि
    वृद्धिवृत्तिप्रयुक्तम् भवति असत्यम् ।
    अग्रिममूल्याङ्क भवति ० ।
    अग्रिमपर्वाङ्क भवति ० ।
    वृत्तिसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    पर्वसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    आज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    ॰ `W-xmodule`: THE CURSOR ONLY, and the arena is deliberately not cleared —
    ॰ every reader walks `१ ..= बाह्यसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क` and so cannot see a previous
    ॰ program's tail. Clearing the run as well would be free here and is left
    ॰ undone on purpose: the invariant that matters is the WALK's bound, and a
    ॰ reader that trusts `दैर्घ्य` is wrong whether or not this line tidies up.
    ॰ That mistake cost this row a full census: `यन्त्रमण्डलरचनामस्ति` walked
    ॰ `आज्ञाकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य` and read the module before it.
    बाह्यसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    वर्तमानपर्व भवति पर्वाङ्कनम् ० ।
    वर्तमानारम्भाज्ञा भवति ० ।
    वाक्यविरामः भवति ० ।
    आदानसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    पाठाक्षरसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    ॰ `W-278`: the module's globals, cleared with everything else. A cursor
    ॰ reset without its arena is the leak this project has paid for twice — the
    ॰ arenas keep their old rows and the cursor is the clear, which holds only
    ॰ because every reader walks to the CURSOR and never to `दैर्घ्य`.
    वैश्विकसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    अनिर्णीताह्वानमस्ति भवति असत्यम् ।
    अनिर्णीताह्वानचिह्नकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    स्थानीयसंख्यान भवति ० ।
    अनामस्थलारम्भः भवति ० ।
    ॰ `W-245`: the stub census starts at zero for every cause.
    चरः हेतुः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
