॰ ══════════════ RUN GROWTH, NIL-SAFE LENGTH, CONTENT EQUALITY (2026-09-13) ══════════════
॰ The interpreter grows a run on any index store past its length, reads a nil
॰ run's length as ०, and compares runs by content; compiled code did none of the
॰ three. All of it is built from the kinds already decoded by every twin: blocks,
॰ branches, compares, LoadAt/StoreAt, and the record cursor as a global. Values
॰ that must cross a branch live in anonymous frame slots (अनामस्थानम्).
॰ A POOL OF EIGHT PER ROUTINE (2026-09-13): slots per site put the largest routines
॰ of ir.t1 and vakyavibhaga.t1 over the २०४७-octet frame (FrameTooLarge). The
॰ sequences never nest but one — the length routine inside equality — so each
॰ helper uses fixed indices: growth ०–५, slice ०–४, equality ०–४, length ७.
सार्वजनिक चरः अनामस्थलारम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।    ॰ १ + the pool's first slot, ० = not yet cut
