॰ Content equality of two runs whose elements are विस्तार octets wide: equal
॰ lengths, then every octet. Answers १ or ०.
॰ ॥ AN INDEX READ OF A NIL RUN ANSWERS ०, IT DOES NOT DEREFERENCE ० ॥
॰ (2026-09-14, clause ten, found by rung 75 and not by any test.)
॰ `खण्डदैर्घ्यरचना` above guards a zero base and answers `दैर्घ्यफलम् + (दैर्घ्यफलम्
॰ == ०)` for a non-octet run, so a FRESH run's length reads १ natively — the
॰ interpreter's hole at index ० reproduced on purpose. The READ had no such
॰ guard: it scaled and loaded from a base of ०, so the run claimed one element
॰ and faulted on reaching it. `BadAccess { addr: 0 }` against an interpreted
॰ 5111. The length was made to agree with the interpreter and the read was not.
॰ The corpus RELIES on the pair agreeing: `स्थानविन्यासः`'s own margin says "an
॰ arena cannot be empty — `भवति ०` gives one slot — and a program with no
॰ instruction wants exactly that one slot holding ०".
॰ Slot ६ is the one free scratch (०-५ and ७ are taken). A nested read —
॰ `अ अङ्कः अ अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः अन्तः` — is safe on one slot because the inner
॰ read is fully built, joined and consumed into a value before the outer's
॰ store to the slot is emitted; the windows do not overlap.
