॰ ॥ GROWTH ॥ before an index store: if the run is nil or its capacity (octets, at
॰ base − १६) is below (index + १) × विस्तार, a new block of need + २ × old capacity
॰ octets is cut from the record region, the header written, the old elements
॰ copied by words, and the new base left in वृद्धिनवाधाराङ्कः with the current
॰ block being the write-back block — the caller stores the new base into the
॰ run's own location, then calls खण्डवृद्धिसमाप्तिः, which raises the length to
॰ index + १ when the index is at or past it. The old block is not reclaimed.
