॰ THE RUST ORIGINAL IS ITSELF MOSTLY A STUB AND SAYS SO — its Identifier
॰ arm comments "Stub: returning 0 for unmapped identifiers" and its
॰ catch-all comments "Stub everything else to 0". Both are ported as
॰ written, comment and all, because porting a stub as a stub is faithful
॰ and quietly improving it here would put the two files out of step.
॰
॰ वास्तु carries three expression kinds the Rust AST does not have —
॰ क्षेत्र (member access), आह्वान (call) and द्विकर्म (binary operator).
॰ क्षेत्र still falls into the catch-all, as it does in Rust's `_` arm.
॰ आह्वान stopped doing so with `W-204` — see its arm.
॰
॰ द्विकर्म NO LONGER DOES, and this margin argued for two cycles that it
॰ should — "inventing an arm Rust has not got makes this file the origin of
॰ a behaviour rather than the port of one". THE ARGUMENT WAS ABOUT THE
॰ WRONG THING. `ir.rs:23-25` DECLARES Add and Sub and constructs NEITHER,
॰ so the instructions are the original's and only the join is new; and the
॰ cost of leaving the join out was not a missing feature but a WRONG ONE,
॰ because the catch-all below does not refuse an unported kind — it emits a
॰ ध्रुवाज्ञा holding ०. measure_corpus_ir read 11 files BUILT while every
॰ `अ योगः आ` in all eleven had lowered to a constant zero. Fidelity to a
॰ port is worth a gap; it is not worth wrong code that runs.

