    ॰ operands are arena indices and `द्विकर्म` names one of `ast.t1`'s FIFTEEN
    ॰ operator kinds (thirteen at :37-49 plus शेष and बृहत्सम at :65-66; the
    ॰ header of this file and `ast.t1:124` both still say thirteen).
    ॰
    ॰ ALL FIFTEEN ARE LOWERED HERE since `W-245`. This arm lowered two for a
    ॰ cycle — योग and वियोग, the two kinds आज्ञा declared — and fell through for
    ॰ the other thirteen to the stub below rather than picking a near
    ॰ neighbour: emitting an Add for a गुणनम् would be `W-195`'s correction
    ॰ (2), an unported kind that silently builds WRONG CODE. The refusal is
    ॰ kept in a different form: every operator has its OWN kind now (the
    ॰ eight operator kinds and तुलना above), so no operator is ever rounded.
    ॰ The five comparisons are ONE kind with a sub-kind — `अधिकम्` is न्यून
    ॰ with the operands exchanged, which is why दक्षिण goes first for it.
    ॰
    ॰ ORDER IS NOT FREE. Instructions are APPENDED, so वाम is built before
    ॰ दक्षिण and both before the operator that consumes them — the same reason
    ॰ the समूह arm below walks in written order rather than in reverse.
