                इति अन्यथा आदि
                    ॰ the resolver's own exception — a qualified name it took
                    ॰ on trust. Bounds-guarded as अङ्कमूल्यम् guards the same read.
                    यदि आह्वेयचिह्नकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
                        यदि आह्वेयचिह्नकाङ्क न्यूनम् आरभ्य पदविभागॱचिह्नकसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
                            चरः चिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः आह्वेयचिह्नकाङ्क अन्तः ।
                            चरः नामपाठ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः चिह्नकम् ।
                            चरः उपसर्गः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱमण्डलउपसर्गः नामपाठ ।
                            यदि उपसर्गः ॱ दैर्घ्य अधिकम् ० आदि
                                स्वीकृतम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                                ॰ `W-xmodule`: MINT AND PUBLISH. The module is
                                ॰ already in hand — `मण्डलउपसर्गः` was called two
                                ॰ lines up for the acceptance test and answers the
                                ॰ part before `ॱ`. The routine is the rest, past
                                ॰ the mark's three octets (U+0971 is E0 A5 B1).
                                ॰ Nothing new is extracted; what was computed to
                                ॰ ACCEPT the callee is now also recorded.
                                चरः बाह्यादिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य उपसर्गः ॱ दैर्घ्य योगः ३ समाप्तम् ।
                                चरः बाह्यदैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य नामपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य वियोगः बाह्यादिः समाप्तम् ।
                                यदि बाह्यदैर्घ्यम् अधिकम् ० आदि
                                    ॰ ══ `खण्डपाठः`'s THIRD PARAMETER IS A BOUND, NOT A LENGTH ══
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ `lex.t1:511` declares it `सीमा` and `:514` proves it absolute:
                                    ॰ `चरः मानम् भवति सीमा वियोगः आरम्भः`. Passing the LENGTH computed
                                    ॰ one line above made the callee compute
                                    ॰ `(total − आदिः) − आदिः` = `total − 2×आदिः`, which for a callee whose
                                    ॰ module and routine names are the same text is `L − (L+3)` = **−3**.
                                    ॰ Its `यावत्` never runs, `फलम्` stays at its declared ०, and an EMPTY
                                    ॰ run comes back WITH NO ERROR ANYWHERE.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ THE RULE IT PRODUCED: a callee's routine name survived only when it
                                    ॰ was more than 3 octets LONGER than its module name —
                                    ॰ `व्याकरॱकार्यक्रमपठनम्` +21 lived, `पदविभागॱपदविभाग` −3 and
                                    ॰ `अक्षरकोशॱसङ्ख्या` −6 came back empty.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ AND EVERY STAGE AFTER IT WAS SILENT. The guard above tests the
                                    ॰ LENGTH, so it passes; `:2125` writes a correct module; `:2126`
                                    ॰ writes the empty name; `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन`'s copy loop skips exactly the
                                    ॰ empty-named entries; the emitter's lookup misses and answers
                                    ॰ `यन्त्रानामसंज्ञानिषेधभेद` — a refusal whose margin calls itself
                                    ॰ intended, for the type-symbol case this is NOT.
                                    ॰ Measured 2026-09-15: SEVEN corpus sources stopped at hop 0 this way,
                                    ॰ carrying most of the corpus's routines.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ `artha.t1:866-868` does the same split correctly three lines apart
                                    ॰ in shape — `नामदैर्घ्यम् भवति नाम ॱ दैर्घ्य`, the whole length AS THE
                                    ॰ BOUND. This site subtracted first. Written as start-plus-length
                                    ॰ rather than `नामपाठ ॱ दैर्घ्य` so the site states the unit it means.
                                    चरः बाह्यवृत्तिनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱखण्डपाठः नामपाठ बाह्यादिः आरभ्य बाह्यादिः योगः बाह्यदैर्घ्यम् समाप्तम् ।
                                    ॰ ONE SYMBOL PER CALLEE, NOT PER CALL SITE — and the
                                    ॰ scan that makes it so is `बाह्यसंज्ञाग्रहणम्`, shared
                                    ॰ with the FOLDED spaced shape above so that the two
                                    ॰ spellings of one callee cannot mint two symbols.
                                    आह्वेयसंज्ञा भवति बाह्यसंज्ञाग्रहणम् आरभ्य उपसर्गः ऽ बाह्यवृत्तिनाम समाप्तम् ।
                                इति
                            इति
                        इति
                    इति
                इति
            इति
            यदि आह्वेयः ॱ भेद समम् वास्तुॱक्षेत्राभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
                ॰ ॥ A FIELD IS NOT A CALLEE, AND THIS ARM NOW REFUSES ONE ॥
                ॰ `W-280` left this site accepting-without-minting and asked for a
                ॰ case before a repair; the case is in hand (2026-09-18) and it is
                ॰ not a mint.
                ॰
                ॰ WHAT THE ARM WAS WRITTEN FOR IT NO LONGER SEES. Its old margin
                ॰ said *"`मण्डल ॱ वृत्तिः` — the base must be a name the resolver
                ॰ placed (the import)"*. `W-228` (b) took that shape away from it:
                ॰ `parse.t1:945` FOLDS a spaced qualifier whose head names an
                ॰ IMPORTED module into the head's own नाम node, so
                ॰ `सङ्केतन ॱ क्षेत्रसंख्या` never becomes a क्षेत्र at all and is named
                ॰ by the नाम arm above. That is not read off the source: it is
                ॰ falsifiable by a test that already exists and is already green —
                ॰ `w280-folded-callee.rs`'s two-spelling test asserts BOTH spellings
                ॰ carry a symbol, and it reds the moment the spaced form arrives here.
                ॰
                ॰ SO THE ONLY BASE THAT CAN REACH THE ACCEPT IS ONE THE FOLD
                ॰ DECLINED — a record, a parameter, a local, or a head that already
                ॰ carries a member — and T1 has no function values, so none of them
                ॰ names a routine. The old accept wrote `स्वीकृतम् भवति सत्यम्` with
                ॰ `आह्वेयसंज्ञा` still at the ० of its declaration, and
                ॰ `आह्वानाज्ञायोजनम्` appended a Call with `संज्ञा ०` —
                ॰ `यन्त्रनामान्वेषणम् ०` misses it and `यन्त्राह्वानोत्सर्जनम्` refuses
                ॰ the WHOLE MODULE with `यन्त्रानामसंज्ञानिषेधभेद`, a link error a long
                ॰ way from its cause. The refusal below names the call's own token.
                ॰
                ॰ THE CASE, MEASURED AND NOT ARGUED (2026-09-18). A record-typed
                ॰ parameter's field applied to an argument — `र ॱ क ७` — reaches this
                ॰ arm, and before this change it built exactly ONE Call with
                ॰ `संज्ञा ०`. AND THE CORPUS CANNOT SEE THE DIFFERENCE: all 21
                ॰ sources driven to built IR on a fresh interpreter each carry ZERO
                ॰ क्षेत्र-shaped callees — not zero UNNAMED ones, zero of the SHAPE —
                ॰ so this accept was dead for every source that ships. The census in
                ॰ `w280-folded-callee.rs` now counts that shape and reports it, so a
                ॰ source that begins to reach this refusal SAYS SO instead of
                ॰ appearing as a call that stopped being built.
                ॰
                ॰ NOT MINTED, which is the half the old margin had right: a synthetic
                ॰ `बाह्यसंज्ञा` for a record's field would name a label no module
                ॰ exports — the same link error under another name.
                ॰
                ॰ `आह्वेयमस्ति` STAYS सत्यम् ON PURPOSE. The refusal below is guarded
                ॰ by it; dropping it instead would fall through to the
                ॰ `अपूर्णध्रुवम् १४` stub at the foot, which appends nothing AND
                ॰ records nothing — silence where a named refusal belongs.
                आह्वेयमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
                आह्वेयचिह्नकाङ्क भवति आह्वेयः ॱ मूल्यसूचकाङ्क ।
            इति
        इति

        ॰ THE REFUSAL, before anything is appended for this call.
        यदि आह्वेयमस्ति समम् सत्यम् आदि
            यदि स्वीकृतम् समम् असत्यम् आदि
                यदि अनिर्णीताह्वानमस्ति समम् असत्यम् आदि
                    अनिर्णीताह्वानमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
                    अनिर्णीताह्वानचिह्नकाङ्क भवति आह्वेयचिह्नकाङ्क ।
                इति
                प्रत्यागमनम् मूल्याङ्कनम् ० ।
            इति
        इति

        ॰ र — the arguments out: built in written order onto the scratch
        ॰ stack, then moved to आदानकोश as one contiguous run. Only for a
        ॰ shape this arm reads; the index shape falls to the stub below.
        यदि आह्वेयमस्ति समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः आदानगणना ॱॱ न६४ भवति आह्वानादानरचना अभिसूचकाङ्क ।
        चरः आदानारम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य आदानसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
        चरः सञ्चयाधारः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क वियोगः आदानगणना समाप्तम् ।
        ॰ ॥ THE STORE, INSTEAD OF THE CALL ॥ Taken BEFORE the argument loop so no
        ॰ operand is appended to a call that is never emitted; the arguments are
        ॰ already evaluated into `आदानसञ्चयकोश` and the cursor is popped here as
        ॰ the loop would pop it. Answers ० — the same value the interpreter's own
        ॰ interception answers — so a caller cannot tell which side handled it,
        ॰ and `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्`'s body answers २६८४३५४५६ if NEITHER did.
        यदि मुद्रणमिदम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            चरः यन्त्रस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४३५४५६ ।
            चरः अष्टकमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनयन्त्रनिधान ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य यन्त्रस्थानम् ऽ अष्टकमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति सञ्चयाधारः ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् ध्रुवरचना ० ।
        इति
        ॰ ॥ THE FILE WINDOW, THE SAME SHAPE AT A DIFFERENT ADDRESS ॥ २६८४४३६४८ is
        ॰ ०x१००० २०००, and the value stored is the caller's SIX-WORD REQUEST RUN —
        ॰ a run's runtime value IS its pointer, which is why this intrinsic takes
        ॰ one: `.t1` has no address-of, so an `न६४` parameter would have been
        ॰ uncallable. The host reads the request
        ॰ out of RAM and writes its status back into RAM before this store returns,
        ॰ so nothing here has to represent "not yet"; ADR-0040's question does not
        ॰ arise, and this channel is correspondingly no use for a socket.
        ॰ Answers ० exactly as the print arm does; `अष्टकॱपत्रम्`'s body answers
        ॰ २६८४४३६४८ if this lowering is ever removed.
        यदि पत्रमिदम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            ॰ THREE STORES, AND THE ORDER IS THE PROTOCOL. The path and the
            ॰ buffer are only REMEMBERED by the host; the third store is the one
            ॰ that reads the file, so a half-built request never reaches a
            ॰ filesystem. Each value is a RUN's pointer, which is what makes this
            ॰ callable from a program at all: `.t1` has no address-of, and a run
            ॰ already carries its pointer.
            चरः मार्गस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६४८ ।
            चरः मार्गमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनमार्गनिधान ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य मार्गस्थानम् ऽ मार्गमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            चरः पात्रस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६५६ ।
            चरः पात्रमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः २ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनपात्रनिधान ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य पात्रस्थानम् ऽ पात्रमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            चरः स्थितिस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६६४ ।
            चरः स्थितिमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः ३ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनस्थितिनिधान ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य स्थितिस्थानम् ऽ स्थितिमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति सञ्चयाधारः ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् ध्रुवरचना ० ।
        इति
        ॰ THE WRITE — identical but for the third address. २६८४४३६७२ is
        ॰ ०x१००० २०१८; the path and the buffer are remembered by the same two
        ॰ stores, and only the go differs.
        यदि पत्रलेखनमिदम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            चरः लेमार्गस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६४८ ।
            चरः लेमार्गमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः १ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनलेमार्ग ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य लेमार्गस्थानम् ऽ लेमार्गमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            चरः लेपात्रस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६५६ ।
            चरः लेपात्रमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः २ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनलेपात्र ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य लेपात्रस्थानम् ऽ लेपात्रमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            चरः लेस्थितिस्थानम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति ध्रुवरचना २६८४४३६७२ ।
            चरः लेस्थितिमूल्यम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः आरभ्य सञ्चयाधारः योगः ३ समाप्तम् अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनलेस्थिति ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थाननिधानरचना आरभ्य लेस्थितिस्थानम् ऽ लेस्थितिमूल्यम् समाप्तम् ।
            आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति सञ्चयाधारः ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् ध्रुवरचना ० ।
        इति
        चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
        यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य आदानगणना योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
            चरः सञ्चितम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति आदानसञ्चयकोश अङ्कः सञ्चयाधारः योगः क्रमः अन्तः ।
            चरः अवगणनादान ॱॱ न६४ भवति आदानयोजनम् सञ्चितम् ।
            क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
        इति
        आदानसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क भवति सञ्चयाधारः ।

        ॰ ट — the call; व — the value at the site control returns to. Named
        ॰ `आह्वानफलम्` and not `फलम्`: this routine's catch-all declares `फलम्`
        ॰ after the arms, and `W-222`'s ratchet reads a use-then-redeclare of
        ॰ one name in one routine as two meanings — legal, and avoided here.
        चरः आह्वानफलम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति नवमूल्यम् ० ।
        चरः अवगणनाह्वान ॱॱ न६४ भवति आह्वानाज्ञायोजनम् आरभ्य आह्वानफलम् ऽ आह्वेयसंज्ञा ऽ आदानारम्भः ऽ आदानगणना समाप्तम् ।
        ॰ `W-237`: the callee NODE beside the instruction, for the census —
        ॰ see the side tables above. आह्वेयाङ्क is the node the walk stopped
        ॰ on: a name, or the क्षेत्र of the spaced qualified form.
        आह्वेयकोश अङ्कः अवगणनाह्वान अन्तः भवति आह्वेयाङ्क ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् आह्वानफलम् ।
        इति
        ॰ the index shape — W-228's slice read as a call; counted, `W-245`.
        प्रत्यागमनम् अपूर्णध्रुवम् १४ ।
    इति

    ॰ ── THE नाम ARM — `W-237`, closing (d) at the foot. ──
    ॰ A ROUTINE'S BARE NAME IN VALUE POSITION IS A CALL WITH NO ARGUMENTS.
    ॰ `parse.t1` pushes one आह्वान node per ARGUMENT, so `प्रत्यागमनम् आरम्भः ।`
    ॰ reaches this routine as a नामाभिव्यञ्जक and, until this arm, took the
    ॰ Identifier stub below: every zero-argument call in the corpus lowered to
    ॰ a constant ० that ran. What tells `आरम्भः` from `क` is not on the node —
    ॰ both carry a symbol — but on the SYMBOL: `W-228` gave `अर्थ` an arena of
    ॰ kinds by SymbolId+१, and kind १ is `व्याकर`'s वृत्तिघोषणाभेद, a routine.
    ॰ So the node's संज्ञासूचकाङ्क leads to that arena, and a routine kind here
    ॰ is a Call with संज्ञा the symbol and an EMPTY argument run — the same
    ॰ आह्वानाज्ञायोजनम् the arm above appends, with a count of ०. A चरः, a
    ॰ parameter, an import, an unresolved name (०): the stub, as before.
    ॰ BOUNDS-GUARDED as अङ्कमूल्यम् guards its read: a symbol past the arena's
    ॰ length was declared by a caller that set no kind, and reading it would be
    ॰ an error rather than a शून्यम्. MEASURED before writing (W-208): such
    ॰ sites are the `args` bucket ० of the call census. ir.rs's twin is the
    ॰ `routines` table its `build_program` fills in a pass of its own.
    ॰ ── A LOCAL OR A PARAMETER FIRST — `W-245`. ── The routine in hand
    ॰ declared the name (its parameters at entry, its `चरः` as the body
    ॰ reached them), so the value is a LOAD from the name's slot, whatever
    ॰ symbol the resolver placed: the innermost declaration wins there too.
    यदि अभि ॱ भेद समम् वास्तुॱनामाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        चरः नामचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः अभि ॱ मूल्यसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
        चरः स्थानीयस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति स्थानीयस्थानम् आरभ्य पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः नामचिह्नकम् समाप्तम् ।
        यदि स्थानीयस्थलम् अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः आहारफलम् ॱॱ मूल्याङ्क भवति नवमूल्यम् ० ।
            चरः अवगणनाहार ॱॱ न६४ भवति आहाराज्ञायोजनम् आरभ्य आहारफलम् ऽ आरभ्य स्थानीयस्थलम् वियोगः १ समाप्तम् समाप्तम् ।
            रचितगणनम् २ ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् आहारफलम् ।
        इति
    इति

    यदि अभि ॱ भेद समम् वास्तुॱनामाभिव्यञ्जकभेद आदि
        चरः नामसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति अभि ॱ संज्ञासूचकाङ्क ।
        चरः नामभेदः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
        यदि नामसंज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
            यदि नामसंज्ञा न्यूनम् अर्थॱसंज्ञाभेदकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
                नामभेदः भवति अर्थॱसंज्ञाभेदकोश अङ्कः नामसंज्ञा अन्तः ।
                ॰ A SLOT INSIDE THE LENGTH CAN STILL BE `शून्यम्`, and the length
                ॰ guard above does not catch it. `अर्थ` HAS TWO MINTERS AND ONLY
                ॰ ONE OF THEM FILLS ALL THREE symbol-keyed arenas.
                ॰ `संज्ञाग्रहणम्` (`artha.t1:1246`) mints the SymbolId and advances
                ॰ the counter, and it has exactly two callers: `घोषणम्` (`:1265`),
                ॰ which writes the type, the KIND and the declaration at `:1271`,
                ॰ `:1273`, `:1275`, and `सञ्चयसंज्ञा` (`:1948`), which interns a
                ॰ CROSS-MODULE member and writes the type ALONE at `:1963`. So
                ॰ every store member advances the counter while filling one arena
                ॰ of three, the next `घोषणम्` writes at a higher index, and the
                ॰ interpreter's sparse write pads the gap with `Nil`. The type
                ॰ arena has both writers and is therefore dense; the kind and the
                ॰ declaration have one each and are the two that carry holes.
                ॰ Reading a hole put `शून्यम्` in this `न६४` local, and the
                ॰ two tests below then behaved differently: `समम् ०` compares two
                ॰ values and answers false without complaint, while `बृहत्समम् ७`
                ॰ is an ORDERING and asks the interpreter for a number, which
                ॰ raised "expected a number, found Nil" and stopped the build.
                ॰ MEASURED 2026-09-05, merging this lane onto main: ELEVEN of the
                ॰ fifteen corpus sources stopped at IR — and only against a census
                ॰ that COLLECTS (`W-253`), because a filled store is what mints
                ॰ the symbols whose kind slot is a hole. This lane's own census
                ॰ built a fresh interpreter per source and could not reach the
                ॰ path. A hole means NO KIND, which is what ० already means here.
                ॰ THIS GUARD IS PERMANENT AND OUTLIVES THE WRITER'S REPAIR — the
                ॰ amendment that makes `सञ्चयसंज्ञा` write all three arenas does
                ॰ NOT retire it. Belt-and-braces, and the reason is not doubt
                ॰ about that repair: a reader that treats "inside the length" as
                ॰ "written" is wrong however well the invariant is kept, and here
                ॰ it is kept by CONVENTION — nothing refuses a third minter that
                ॰ fills one arena, and it would reintroduce every hole in silence.
                ॰ What such a reader gets is not a wrong answer at the read but a
                ॰ build halting with "expected a number, found Nil" some distance
                ॰ away, which is how this one was found. Guard at the read.
                यदि नामभेदः समम् शून्यम् आदि
                    नामभेदः भवति ० ।
                इति
                ॰ ॥ A MODULE-LEVEL `चरः` READ — `W-278` ॥
                ॰
                ॰ Lowered to `LoadGlobal`, which loads the word at the global's
                ॰ own exported label. UNIFORM: it does not matter whether
                ॰ anything writes the global. The optimisation that would matter
                ॰ — a global nothing assigns is a constant, so fold it — CANNOT
                ॰ BE DECIDED HERE: `कार्यक्रमरचना` walks `व्याकरॱघोषणाकोश`, the
                ॰ declarations of ONE source, so a write performed by another
                ॰ module is invisible. All 541 module-level globals in the corpus
                ॰ are `सार्वजनिक` and none is private, so no candidate could be
                ॰ proven unwritten from its own source either. Folding wrongly
                ॰ freezes the global at its initialiser and every read answers ०
                ॰ — a WRONG ANSWER, not a crash.
                ॰
                ॰ ONLY A SCALAR. An arena global's value is an ADDRESS, not the
                ॰ word at one, so it keeps a stub under its own cause. The test
                ॰ is `अर्थ`'s own type for the symbol, which `सञ्चयसंज्ञा` writes
                ॰ for a cross-module member too — so this works for a global
                ॰ another module declared, where the local declaration arena
                ॰ would hold nothing.
                यदि नामभेदः समम् व्याकरॱचरघोषणाभेद आदि
                    ॰ ONLY A GLOBAL THIS SOURCE DECLARES. A cross-module global
                    ॰ read would emit a reference to a label THIS IMAGE MAY NOT
                    ॰ CONTAIN — the storage is laid by the declaring module, and
                    ॰ that module's object is only linked in if something else
                    ॰ pulled it in. Measured: lowering those too took the corpus
                    ॰ from 15 assembled to 2, with the linker naming labels like
                    ॰ `सङ्केतनक्षेत्रारम्भः` as UNRESOLVED.
                    ॰ `संज्ञाघोषणाकोश` is ० for a member `सञ्चयसंज्ञा` interned
                    ॰ from the store and non-zero for a declaration `घोषणम्`
                    ॰ made here, so it is exactly the "declared in this source"
                    ॰ test — the same arena `W-274` established has one writer.
                    चरः घोषणास्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
                    यदि नामसंज्ञा न्यूनम् अर्थॱसंज्ञाघोषणाकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
                        चरः घोषितम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति अर्थॱसंज्ञाघोषणाकोश अङ्कः नामसंज्ञा अन्तः ।
                        ॰ `असमम् ०` first: a ० is already what घोषणास्थलम् holds, so
                        ॰ skipping it changes nothing, and no ० is compared with a hole.
                        यदि घोषितम् असमम् ० आदि
                            यदि घोषितम् असमम् शून्यम् आदि
                                घोषणास्थलम् भवति घोषितम् ।
                            इति
                        इति
                    इति
                    ॰ ═══ THIS REFUSAL IS NOT GUARD B'S, AND ४४ SAYS SO ═══
                    ॰
                    ॰ Cause २४ was raised here AND at the type-arena guard below,
                    ॰ and its name — `name_global_arena` — describes only that one.
                    ॰ This site refuses for a different reason with a different
                    ॰ owner: the declaration-site slot read as ०. Same shape as
                    ॰ `W-field-split` on cause २५, and the same sentence: one
                    ॰ number credits the row with the smaller residue while
                    ॰ hiding the larger.
                    ॰
                    ॰ ॥ ० HERE IS ALWAYS A WRITTEN ० ॥ and that is DERIVED, not
                    ॰ observed. The two ways a sentinel could reach this test —
                    ॰ the index past the arena's length, or a `शून्यम्` slot — are
                    ॰ both closed by structure. `:1705` above has already read the
                    ॰ KIND out of `संज्ञाभेदकोश` at this same index and found it
                    ॰ equal to a declaration kind; an equality against `शून्यम्`
                    ॰ ANSWERS FALSE rather than faulting, so a hole diverts the
                    ॰ name to another arm and never arrives here. And the two
                    ॰ arenas are written in LOCKED PAIRS — `artha.t1:1790`/`:1792`
                    ॰ and `:2629`/`:2630`, identical index expression, adjacent,
                    ॰ same block depth — so their lengths are equal and their
                    ॰ holes coincide. No index can be inside one and outside the
                    ॰ other. A third cause for "no declaration recorded" would be
                    ॰ UNRAISEABLE, and a declared-but-never-raised row is the
                    ॰ silent half of the numbered-table trap.
                    ॰
                    ॰ ॥ ४४ STILL HOLDS AT LEAST TWO POPULATIONS ॥ and it is named
                    ॰ for what is OBSERVED — the slot read as ० — rather than for
                    ॰ the cause anyone infers from it. `घोष्यमाणघोषणा` is reset to
                    ॰ ० at `artha.t1:1794` after every declaration and set in one
                    ॰ place only, `:1908`; of the three `घोषणम्` callers only
                    ॰ `:1984` shares that setter's innermost block, so `:2086` and
                    ॰ `:2248` store ० for names that are NOT cross-module. So a ०
                    ॰ here is a cross-module member — honest, by `:1713` — OR an
                    ॰ in-module name whose declaration index was never recorded,
                    ॰ which is a GAP IN अर्थ. Those want opposite repairs and the
                    ॰ discriminator is one condition at this site. Naming this
                    ॰ `_foreign` would have repeated the very error the split
                    ॰ exists to undo.
                    ॰
                    ॰ ॥ THIS LOWERS NOTHING ॥ Every name that reached a stub still
                    ॰ reaches one. `paradigm_ir_stubs` MUST NOT MOVE and २४+४४
                    ॰ must sum to what २४ alone counted. A FALL would mean a site
                    ॰ stopped being counted, not that one was fixed.
                    ॰
                    ॰ ४४ because the code space was ENUMERATED FROM ITS STORAGE:
                    ॰ the literal raises across `crates/sadhana-t1/src/*.t1` run to
                    ॰ ४३, and २८/२९ — the obvious pick from the first screen of
                    ॰ `STUB_CAUSES` — are TAKEN by the field-qualified family. A
                    ॰ truncated table reads exactly like a complete one.
                    चरः प्रकारसूचकः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
                    यदि नामसंज्ञा न्यूनम् अर्थॱसंज्ञाप्रकारकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
                        प्रकारसूचकः भवति अर्थॱसंज्ञाप्रकारकोश अङ्कः नामसंज्ञा अन्तः ।
                        ॰ A slot inside the length can still be `शून्यम्` — the
                        ॰ same hole guard as the kind read above, and for the
                        ॰ same reason.
                        यदि प्रकारसूचकः असमम् ० आदि
                            यदि प्रकारसूचकः समम् शून्यम् आदि
                                प्रकारसूचकः भवति ० ।
                            इति
                        इति
                    इति
                    ॰ THE LOWERING HALF OF वास्तु, 2026-09-13. A cross-module global read has
                    ॰ घोषणास्थलम् ० — its declaration lives in another module's arenas — and
                    ॰ this arm refused it (cause 44) BEFORE asking the checker for its type.
                    ॰ The load never needed the declaration site: वैश्विकाज्ञाभेद carries
                    ॰ नामसंज्ञा, the emitter turns that symbol into the declaring module's
                    ॰ exported label, and the data-only objects (ast.t1, vastu.t1) export every
                    ॰ global. So the type is looked up FIRST, and cause 44 is raised only when
                    ॰ the checker has no type for the symbol either.
                    यदि घोषणास्थलम् समम् ० आदि
                        यदि प्रकारसूचकः समम् ० आदि
                            प्रत्यागमनम् अपूर्णध्रुवम् ४४ ।
                        इति
                    इति
                    यदि प्रकारसूचकः अधिकम् ० आदि
                        यदि प्रकारसूचकः न्यूनम् अर्थॱअर्थप्रकारकोश ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
