                                ॰
                                ॰ `W-293`, defect 1. The symbol stays ONE POINTER
                                ॰ WORD — the emitter now lays a relocated pointer
                                ॰ beside reserved space rather than a bare quad —
                                ॰ so a run's base is READ FROM THAT WORD, which is
                                ॰ an ordinary `वैश्विकाज्ञाभेद`. Nothing about the
                                ॰ access path changes, which is why the four proven
                                ॰ LOCAL cells are the control for this edit.
                                ॰
                                ॰ NO NEW KIND AND NO NEW SHAPE NUMBER, so
                                ॰ `रचितशेषसीमा` DOES NOT RISE, and that is
                                ॰ deliberate rather than forgotten: a run's read
                                ॰ raises the SAME shape २६ an integer's does,
                                ॰ because it is the same instruction on the same
                                ॰ word. An absent bound-bump reads as an oversight
                                ॰ to every later reader; this sentence is the only
                                ॰ thing that distinguishes the two.
