        ॰ `W-284` — THE ONLY LINE THAT DIFFERS BETWEEN A READ AND A WRITE. Every
        ॰ guard above, the `विस्तार` check included, has already run and refused
        ॰ the same set for both. The index was scaled by the width two lines up,
        ॰ so `सूचीस्थान` २६ receives a BYTE COUNT and its emitter must not scale
        ॰ again — said in the emitter's margin too, because a doubled stride is
        ॰ a legal address and nothing downstream would object.
        यदि स्थानमात्रमिदम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            चरः अवगणनसूचीस्थान ॱॱ न६४ भवति आज्ञायोजनम् आरभ्य सूचीस्थानाज्ञाभेद ऽ सूचीफलान्तिमम् ऽ ० ऽ ० ऽ आधारफलम् ऽ अन्तरफलम् ऽ ० समाप्तम् ।
            रचितगणनम् ३२ ।
            ॰ `W-len` — THE HIGH-WATER BUMP, AND THIS BRANCH IS THE ONLY PLACE
            ॰ IT CAN GO. It needs the BASE and the element ORDINAL, and the
            ॰ store arms downstream hold neither — an assignment target is
            ॰ lowered with `स्थानमात्रम्` set and what reaches
            ॰ `स्थाननिधानाज्ञाभेद` is one already-computed ADDRESS. Here
            ॰ `आधारफलम्` and `सूचीफलम्` are both live, and `स्थानमात्रम्` is set
            ॰ ONLY for an assignment target, so a bump written here fires on
            ॰ stores and never on reads. That property exists nowhere else in
            ॰ this file.
            ॰
            ॰ THE ORDINAL, NEVER `अन्तरफलम्`. The header counts ELEMENTS; the
            ॰ scaled offset would be wrong by the width for every run whose
            ॰ elements are not eight octets, which `W-narrow` made reachable.
            ॰
            ॰ BRANCH-FREE — `दैर्घ्य भवति दैर्घ्य योगः आरभ्य नव वियोगः दैर्घ्य
            ॰ समाप्तम् गुणनम् अधिकमिति`, which is `max` without a block
            ॰ boundary. A conditional here would put one at EVERY indexed store
            ॰ and reach the block numbering, the label allocator and every
            ॰ reader that walks blocks; ten straight-line instructions over
            ॰ existing kinds touch nothing structural. A `Cmp` read as a VALUE
            ॰ is supported — `riscv64.rs` materialises it as `slt`/`sltu`.
            ॰
            ॰ NO GUARD ON THE BASE, WHICH IS THE DESIGN'S OWN TEST. This arm
            ॰ already refused anything but `खण्डार्थभेद` above, and every run
            ॰ base now carries a header — local allocation, bss global, rodata
            ॰ literal. If a guard is ever needed here, some run's base is being
            ॰ formed without one and the design is incomplete.
