    ॰ Statement::Assign — no `ast.rs` twin; `W-245`. `parse.t1` writes
    ॰ `वाक्ययोजनम्(समवाक्यभेद, वाम, दक्षिण)`, two expressions. A left side that
    ॰ is a NAME this routine holds a slot for is a STORE. Any other left side —
    ॰ a field, an index, a module-level चरः — is COUNTED (causes २०..२३) and
    ॰ stores nothing, while the right side is still built: its calls are real
    ॰ and the interpreter evaluates them too.
    यदि वाक्यम् ॱ भेद समम् वास्तुॱसमवाक्यभेद आदि
