                                    ॰ ॥ THE WRITE ACCEPTS WHAT THE READ ACCEPTS ॥
                                    ॰ This tested `पूर्णाङ्क` ALONE while the read arm
                                    ॰ at `:1822-1828` accepts `पूर्णाङ्क` OR `खण्ड`, so a
                                    ॰ global holding a run could be READ and not
                                    ॰ WRITTEN — and the store fell through to
                                    ॰ `अपूर्णवाक्यम् २२`, a stub, with no diagnostic.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ `W-284`'s rule is the reason this is a defect and
                                    ॰ not a choice: "A READ AND ITS WRITE MUST REFUSE THE
                                    ॰ SAME SET, and the only way to be sure of that is
                                    ॰ for there to be one set." Two type tests that drift
                                    ॰ apart are exactly what that margin forbids, and
                                    ॰ they had drifted.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ WRITTEN AS THE READ'S OWN SHAPE — a `बूल` set by
                                    ॰ two independent tests — rather than as one `अथवा`,
                                    ॰ so that the two arms remain diffable line for line
                                    ॰ and a third type added to one is visibly absent
                                    ॰ from the other.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ NOTHING ELSE MOVES. The address and store emission
                                    ॰ below is untouched, `वैश्विकस्थानाज्ञाभेद` २१ and
                                    ॰ `स्थाननिधानाज्ञाभेद` २३ as before, and shape २९
                                    ॰ `assign_store_global` already existed and is raised
                                    ॰ here — this widens WHICH targets reach it.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ ONE WORD IS THE WHOLE RUN, AND THE READ ARM'S OWN
                                    ॰ MARGIN SAYS WHY. `W-293` at `:1798`: "The symbol
                                    ॰ stays ONE POINTER WORD — the emitter now lays a
                                    ॰ relocated pointer beside reserved space rather than
                                    ॰ a bare quad — so a run's base is READ FROM THAT
                                    ॰ WORD". `खण्डसामर्थ्यम् × ८` is the SPACE; the symbol
                                    ॰ is a pointer to it. So a one-word `स्थाननिधान`
                                    ॰ writes the POINTER and is not a truncated copy.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ IT ALIASES, BY DESIGN, MATCHING THE INTERPRETER.
                                    ॰ `अष्टकदोषनाम भवति नाम` makes the global share
                                    ॰ `नाम`'s run rather than copy it, which is what
                                    ॰ `nirvahana` already does — arenas are
                                    ॰ `Rc<RefCell<Vec>>` there, so assignment is by
                                    ॰ reference on both sides.
                                    ॰
                                    ॰ AND THE SPACE THE OLD POINTER NAMED BECOMES
                                    ॰ UNREACHABLE FROM THIS SYMBOL — a leak, not a wrong
                                    ॰ answer, and the interpreter has the same shape via
                                    ॰ `Rc` drop. Stated because a reader who notices it
                                    ॰ should find it already known rather than think it
                                    ॰ was missed.
                                    चरः लक्ष्यलेख्यम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
                                    यदि लक्ष्यप्रकारः ॱ भेद समम् अर्थॱपूर्णाङ्कार्थभेद आदि
                                        लक्ष्यलेख्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                                    इति
                                    यदि लक्ष्यप्रकारः ॱ भेद समम् अर्थॱखण्डार्थभेद आदि
                                        लक्ष्यलेख्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                                    इति
                                    यदि लक्ष्यप्रकारः ॱ भेद समम् अर्थॱसंरचनार्थभेद आदि
                                        लक्ष्यलेख्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
                                    इति
