                            ॰ A RECORD GLOBAL NEEDS ITS FIELDS (2026-09-14). Only the
                            ॰ slice arm above raised the capacity, so a global of record
                            ॰ type got ONE word — the emitter emits `word → भण्डार` only
                            ॰ above eight octets — and every field read or write went
                            ॰ through address ०. Interpreted the zero value of a record
                            ॰ is a map of zero fields, so it worked there; natively the
                            ॰ first such global reached (`अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः` in the
                            ॰ compression chooser) faulted BadAccess at ० the moment the
                            ॰ assembler first ran with its tables. Three globals in the
                            ॰ corpus have record type; a LOCAL of record type already
                            ॰ allocates in the declaration arm, which is why the rung
                            ॰ separating them reads 9 natively and the global reads a
                            ॰ fault.
