    प्रत्यागमनम् वृत्तिसूचकाङ्क ।
इति


॰ ══════════════════ what is NOT ported, and why ══════════════════
॰
॰ Neither of these is a stub routine. Both are ARMS missing from routines
॰ that otherwise do their whole job, which is why they are written down
॰ here instead of being counted as unimplemented functions — a count of
॰ अपूर्णम् returns would report this file as complete, and it is not.
॰
॰ (a) CLOSED BY `W-194`, AND THIS ENTRY IS KEPT RATHER THAN DELETED
॰     because its stated fix was WRONG and a later reader would otherwise
॰     re-derive it. It read: "वाक्यरचना's समूह arm walks nothing ... the fix
॰     is a child link in वास्तु ॱ वाक्य — a next-sibling index, or a
॰     first/count pair over a third arena — and that is वास्तु's row and
॰     व्याकर's, not this one's." The double-emit it feared is real —
॰     वाक्ययोजनम् numbers a statement AFTER its children, so a nested
॰     block's statements lie inside its parent's range — but NO NEW FIELD
॰     WAS NEEDED. आदिसूचकाङ्क already permits a backward skip, so a scan
॰     from अन्तिम down, keeping the smallest root still above the last
॰     visited, yields the direct children in written order; `अर्थ` had
॰     solved it at artha.t1:990 and the corpus resolves 15/15 on it. The
॰     walk is at the समूह arm above. Nothing in वास्तु changed.
॰
॰ (b) CLOSED BY `W-245` (2026-09-04), KEPT AS (a), (c) AND (d) ARE. It read:
॰     "कार्यक्रमरचना emits no Param instructions. Rust writes `for (i, _) in
॰     params.iter().enumerate()` over Declaration::Function's params field.
॰     व्याकर ॱ घोषणा HAS NO SUCH FIELD: वृत्तिपठनम् reads the parameter list
॰     token by token and keeps nothing — not the count, not the names, not
॰     the types. So the loop has no bound to run to." The field arrived on
॰     2026-09-01 as a RANGE, `प्राचलादि..प्राचलान्त` into `व्याकर ॱ प्राचलकोश`
॰     (a count could not locate the parameters once a second routine had
॰     pushed its own), and the loop is in कार्यक्रमरचना now — a Param and a
॰     Store per parameter — beside the locals table that W-245 added for a
॰     routine's `चरः`. Until this row a parameter read in a body was the
॰     Identifier stub, so every routine computed over constants whatever
॰     it was passed; the census number that moved is the encode census's
॰     `zero_constants`, and its first non-zero finisher status is W-245's.
॰
॰ (c) CLOSED BY `W-204`, KEPT FOR THE SAME REASON AS (a). It read: "आज्ञा ॱ
॰     आदानारम्भ and आदानसंख्यान are declared and written by nothing. They are
॰     Instruction::Call's Vec<ValueId>, and they hold the first index and the
॰     count of a run in a fourth arena that does not exist yet. THAT IS NOT A
॰     REGRESSION: ir.rs constructs no Call either." The fourth arena is
॰     आदानकोश, the arm is the आह्वान arm of अभिव्यञ्जकरचना, and the claim
॰     that it was not a regression was the same mistake the द्विकर्म margin
॰     owns up to: the catch-all did not REFUSE a call, it emitted a
॰     constant ०, so every routine call in the corpus lowered to nothing
॰     and the census read BUILT. ir.rs still constructs no Call, and cannot
॰     until `ast.rs` has a call expression; the twin is kept in step at the
॰     instruction's SHAPE, which its own test now pins by hand as `W-198`
॰     did for the conditional branch.
॰
॰ (d) CLOSED BY `W-237` (2026-09-04), KEPT AS (a) AND (c) ARE. It read: "A
॰     ZERO-ARGUMENT CALL IS AN IDENTIFIER TO THIS BUILDER — see the आह्वान
॰     arm. `parse.t1` pushes one आह्वान node per ARGUMENT, so `आरम्भः`
॰     alone is a name node and takes the Identifier stub. Distinguishing a
॰     routine name from a variable needs the symbol's kind on the node or a
॰     symbol table this module can read; either is a row of its own." The
॰     row was `W-228`, which put the kind on the SYMBOL (`अर्थ ॱ
॰     संज्ञाभेदकोश`), and the नाम arm of अभिव्यञ्जकरचना now reads it: a
॰     routine kind is a Call with an empty argument run, anything else is
॰     still the stub. The corpus number that moved is `measure_corpus_ir`'s
॰     call count, and the census in `crates/yantra/tests/paradigm_encode.rs`
॰     is where those calls reach the machine.
